/* ============================================================================
   RARITY / INTENSITY DECOUPLING, POLARITY BALANCE, AND THE THIN SIDES — v4
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The README says the rarity tier and the intensity level are "genuinely
   independent" axes. Measured across all 7,133 entries, they were not:

                 common  uncommon  distinctive  signature
        i=1         556       154            6          4
        i=2         994      1076           21          6
        i=3          15       669         2349          4
        i=4           8       102            7        712
        i=5           4         5            3        438

   Cramer's V = 0.729, where 1.0 means one axis is a restatement of the other.
   The suite's old test for this asserted only that each of the twenty cells was
   non-empty, which a single trait satisfies — and in four of them, roughly one
   trait was all there was.

   The consequence is not abstract. The specific character the README offers as
   the thing the four-tier system made expressible — "an ordinary person with one
   startling verbal habit" — needs a QUIET SIGNATURE trait, and there were ten in
   the entire bank. Loud commons: twelve. So the oneLoud budget preset, which caps
   signature at 1 and clamps intensity hard, was fighting its own data: the only
   signature traits it could reach were loud ones, which its intensity cap then
   rejected, and report.rarity.signature.unmet fired as a matter of routine.

   This file is the content answer to that, plus three other measured gaps:

   1. QUIET SIGNATURE AND QUIET DISTINCTIVE (i1-i2). Rare is not the same as loud.
      A signature trait is one you would not have thought of and will not see on
      the next sheet; nothing about that requires it to be shouted. Most of the
      most memorable things about real people are small.

   2. LOUD COMMON (i4-i5). The mirror gap, and the easier one to forget: a big,
      obvious, unmissable behaviour that is nevertheless completely ordinary.
      Plenty of people are loud in exactly the same way.

   3. THE THIN VARIANT SIDES. Three categories carry a presentation variant, and
      all three were lopsided about 3.5 : 1 — Egotistical 11 against Insecure 38,
      Shallow 12 against Guarded 37, Unanalytical 11 against Instinctive 43. The
      VARIANT_FLOOR of 0.25 kept the coin from going all one way, but when it did
      land on the thin side it drew from a pool of eleven. The floor's own comment
      calls it "a stopgap for a content gap, deliberately shaped like one"; this
      is the content. Written to match the side-b regexes in PRESENTATION_VARIANTS
      so the tagger picks them up without loosening the patterns.

   4. NEGATIVE INTELLIGENCE AND NEGATIVE REBELLIOUSNESS. Polarity tag counts ran
      289:37 on intel and 266:36 on rebel. polNormalise stops that reading as
      posture on the radar, but it cannot conjure material: polarityFit had almost
      nothing to select on when a user pushed either slider down, so the negative
      half of two whole axes gave materially less trait-level steering than the
      positive half. Every entry here that belongs on the thin side carries the
      tag.

   ids start at 140000.
   ========================================================================== */
const TRAITS_BALANCE = [

/* ================================================================
   1. QUIET SIGNATURE — rare, and small (intensity 1-2)
   ================================================================ */

/* ---------- Vocabulary Traits ---------- */
{id:140001,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Register & Formality Spectrum",trait:"Keeps one formal word",desc:"Speaks plainly except for a single high-register word they never swap out, apparently unaware it stands out.",example:"Yeah, no, it was a shambles, the whole thing was — well. Lamentable.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{form:1}},
{id:140002,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Register & Formality Spectrum",trait:"Formal only in the negative",desc:"Casual throughout, then reaches for stiff, careful phrasing the moment they have to decline something.",example:"Nah, mate, course — oh. I'm afraid that won't be possible.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{form:1,asrt:-1}},
{id:140003,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Register & Formality Spectrum",trait:"Register borrowed from one person",desc:"Their whole vocabulary is ordinary except for a handful of phrasings audibly inherited from someone specific.",example:"It'll do for the moment. That's — my grandmother used to say that.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140004,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Precision & Specificity Level",trait:"Exact about one thing only",desc:"Vague about nearly everything, then unaccountably precise on a single narrow subject.",example:"A while back. Few years? — the ninth of March, quarter past six.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140005,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Precision & Specificity Level",trait:"Corrects only their own numbers",desc:"Lets everyone else's approximations stand and quietly revises their own mid-sentence.",example:"About twenty of them. Twenty-two.",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{intel:1}},
{id:140006,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Precision & Specificity Level",trait:"Gives the range, never the number",desc:"Will not commit to a single figure even when they plainly know it.",example:"Somewhere between four and six. Call it four to six.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{asrt:-1}},
{id:140007,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Phonetic & Auditory Qualities",trait:"One word said the old way",desc:"Fully assimilated accent apart from a single word that still comes out the way it did at home.",example:"It's in the — the garrrage. Garage.",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140008,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Phonetic & Auditory Qualities",trait:"Drops to a murmur on names",desc:"Ordinary speaking volume throughout, then goes quiet on any proper noun.",example:"So I told — <i>(quieter)</i> — Marguerite — that it wasn't going to work.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{vol:-1}},
{id:140009,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Phonetic & Auditory Qualities",trait:"Hums the sentence first",desc:"A brief closed-mouth note on the pitch of the sentence before the words arrive.",example:"Mm — mm. No, I don't think that's right.",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{pace:-1}},
{id:140010,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Abstractness & Sensory Modality",trait:"One sense does all the work",desc:"Every metaphor they reach for comes from the same sense, and they never notice the pattern.",example:"It didn't smell right. The whole arrangement. Something off about it.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140011,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Abstractness & Sensory Modality",trait:"Weather for feelings",desc:"Describes internal states exclusively in meteorological terms, quietly and without comment.",example:"Bit overcast today. Was fine yesterday.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140012,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Abstractness & Sensory Modality",trait:"Abstract about the concrete",desc:"Talks about physical objects in general terms and emotional matters in specifics — exactly the wrong way round.",example:"The item. The chair — the item. And I felt a sort of thin, cold thing behind the sternum.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140013,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Semantic Density & Modifiers",trait:"One adjective, reused",desc:"Has settled on a single modifier that now does the work of a dozen, and applies it without variation.",example:"It's a fine room. Fine chair. He's fine, actually, he's been fine.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140014,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Semantic Density & Modifiers",trait:"Modifies only after the noun",desc:"Puts the qualifier in afterwards, as an afterthought, every time.",example:"There's a road. Narrow one. Old.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140015,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Directness & Literalness",trait:"Answers the literal question",desc:"Responds precisely to what was asked and never to what was meant, without any evident mischief.",example:"\"Can you pass the salt?\" \"Yes.\"",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{intel:1,warm:-1}},
{id:140016,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Directness & Literalness",trait:"States the obvious as news",desc:"Delivers things everyone present can see in the tone of a fresh discovery, quietly.",example:"It's raining. It's actually raining.",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140017,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Pragmatic Focus & Speech Functions",trait:"Thanks before asking",desc:"Puts the gratitude first, so every request arrives pre-accepted.",example:"Thanks for this — could you have it by Thursday.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{asrt:1,man:1}},
{id:140018,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Pragmatic Focus & Speech Functions",trait:"Asks permission to disagree",desc:"Requests the floor before contradicting anyone, every single time.",example:"Can I say something? Sorry. I don't think that's what happened.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{asrt:-1,man:1}},
{id:140019,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Pragmatic Focus & Speech Functions",trait:"Never asks a question outright",desc:"Converts every question into a statement and waits for it to be answered.",example:"I'm wondering about Thursday.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{asrt:-1}},
{id:140020,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Morphological & Structural Lexicon",trait:"Verbs everything, quietly",desc:"Turns nouns into verbs constantly and at low volume, so nobody quite catches it happening.",example:"I'll diary it. Have you actioned the thing.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140021,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Morphological & Structural Lexicon",trait:"Diminutives for everything large",desc:"Applies small-forms to serious matters and full forms to trivial ones.",example:"Bit of a heart thing. Then I had a Significant Sandwich.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140022,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Conceptual Framework & Loanwords",trait:"One loanword, no translation",desc:"Uses a single foreign term constantly, never explains it, and appears not to know an English one exists.",example:"It was all very — gemütlich. You know. Gemütlich.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140023,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Conceptual Framework & Loanwords",trait:"Trade word in the wrong room",desc:"Carries one term from an old job into every context and does not hear it landing oddly.",example:"We should probably sound the bilges on this relationship.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140024,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Temporal Orientation & Tense Usage",trait:"Present tense for the dead",desc:"Speaks about people who are gone in the present tense, and about the living in the past.",example:"Mum takes it with two sugars. My brother was a difficult man.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:1}},
{id:140025,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Temporal Orientation & Tense Usage",trait:"Dates by weather",desc:"Locates every past event by what the weather was doing rather than when it was.",example:"That was the wet spring. Not the hot one, the wet one.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140026,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Affective & Emotional Intensity",trait:"Understates by exactly one step",desc:"Every feeling is reported one notch below its actual size, consistently enough to be a unit of measure.",example:"Mildly inconvenient. <i>(The house had burned down.)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140027,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Affective & Emotional Intensity",trait:"Feeling words only in the negative",desc:"Can say what they don't feel with total fluency and what they do feel not at all.",example:"I'm not upset. I'm not angry about it. I'm not — no.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:-1}},

/* ---------- Dialogue Grammar Traits ---------- */
{id:140028,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Anchors & Fillers",trait:"Filler only before a lie",desc:"Fluent throughout, and reaches for a hesitation marker exclusively when about to say something untrue.",example:"Yes. Yes. Um — yes, I was at home.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{hon:-1}},
{id:140029,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Anchors & Fillers",trait:"Anchors to a name that isn't there",desc:"Addresses an absent third party as though checking with them, quietly, mid-sentence.",example:"We'd want the Tuesday, wouldn't we, Dad. Anyway.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140030,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Anchors & Fillers",trait:"Uses 'right' as a full stop",desc:"Ends clauses with a flat, unquestioning 'right' that expects nothing back.",example:"So I went down there, right. And it was shut, right.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140031,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Disfluencies & Flow",trait:"Stumbles on the true part",desc:"Entirely fluent through the padding and comes apart on the one sentence that matters.",example:"So the meeting ran late and the — the traffic — I. I didn't want to come home.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{hon:1,emo:1}},
{id:140032,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Disfluencies & Flow",trait:"Restarts once, then commits",desc:"Always abandons the first attempt at a sentence and never the second.",example:"I think we — I think we should sell it.",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140033,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Spoken Compression",trait:"Drops the subject, never the object",desc:"Sheds pronouns at the front of sentences and keeps every other word intact.",example:"Went down there. Saw it. Didn't like the look of it.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140034,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Spoken Compression",trait:"Compresses only what they've said before",desc:"Full sentences for new information, telegraphic for anything they have explained once already.",example:"The valve on the second pump is failing. Second pump. Valve.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140035,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Structural Shifts",trait:"Switches to 'you' for their own life",desc:"Narrates their own experience in the second person without ever noticing the swap.",example:"You get to about forty and you realise nobody's coming.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140036,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Structural Shifts",trait:"Passive voice for their own decisions",desc:"Uses active constructions for everything except things they chose to do.",example:"I drove up on the Tuesday. A decision was made to leave.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{hon:-1}},
{id:140037,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Structural Shifts",trait:"Conditional for the certain",desc:"Wraps things they know for a fact in hypothetical grammar.",example:"You'd find, if you looked, that the money's gone. Which it is.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{asrt:-1}},
{id:140038,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Turn-Taking Grammar",trait:"Yields, then finishes anyway",desc:"Genuinely stops for the interrupter, waits them out, and completes the original sentence exactly.",example:"— no, go on. <i>(waits)</i> — as I was saying, the second pump.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{asrt:1,man:1}},
{id:140039,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Turn-Taking Grammar",trait:"Answers the previous question",desc:"Runs one question behind the conversation and never catches up.",example:"\"How's your mother?\" \"Fine, the drive was fine.\"",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140040,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Turn-Taking Grammar",trait:"Never takes the last word",desc:"Will concede the final sentence of any exchange, even one they are winning.",example:"Sure. <i>(and that is the end of it, every time)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{asrt:-1,agr:1}},
{id:140041,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Repetition & Echo Patterns",trait:"Echoes the last two words",desc:"Repeats the tail of whatever was said to them before responding, quietly, as though tasting it.",example:"\"...by Friday.\" \"By Friday. Right.\"",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140042,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Repetition & Echo Patterns",trait:"Repeats only the numbers",desc:"Lets everything else pass and says every figure back exactly once.",example:"\"Four hundred by the ninth.\" \"Four hundred. Ninth.\"",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{intel:1}},

/* ---------- Mannerisms ---------- */
{id:140043,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Micro-Physical Tics",trait:"Checks a watch they stopped wearing",desc:"Turns the bare wrist over at intervals and looks at nothing.",example:"<i>(glances at the wrist, then at the wall)</i>",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140044,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Micro-Physical Tics",trait:"Taps a count of three",desc:"Any nervous tapping resolves in threes, never four, never two.",example:"<i>(tap, tap, tap — pause — tap, tap, tap)</i>",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{disc:1}},
{id:140045,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Micro-Physical Tics",trait:"Blinks on the stressed syllable",desc:"A single blink lands on the emphasised word of every sentence.",example:"It was <i>(blink)</i> Thursday.",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140046,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Eye & Facial Expressions",trait:"Smiles a half-beat late",desc:"The expression arrives correctly and slightly after it should have.",example:"<i>(pause)</i> — ha. Yes. That's funny.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140047,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Eye & Facial Expressions",trait:"Looks at mouths, not eyes",desc:"Holds attention on the speaker's mouth throughout, which reads as intensity and isn't.",example:"<i>(watching the words form rather than the face)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140048,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Eye & Facial Expressions",trait:"Closes eyes to answer",desc:"Shuts them for the duration of their own reply and opens them at the full stop.",example:"<i>(eyes close)</i> No, I don't think so. <i>(eyes open)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140049,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Tactile & Prop Handling",trait:"Straightens one object only",desc:"Ignores general disorder and cannot leave a single specific kind of item crooked.",example:"<i>(squares the one pen against the table edge, leaves the rest of the mess)</i>",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{disc:1}},
{id:140050,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Tactile & Prop Handling",trait:"Warms things in both hands",desc:"Cups whatever they are holding as though it were a mug, whatever it actually is.",example:"<i>(holding the stapler in two hands, thumbs together)</i>",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140051,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Tactile & Prop Handling",trait:"Puts things down soundlessly",desc:"Sets every object down with a deliberateness that makes no noise at all.",example:"<i>(the glass reaches the table without a sound)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{disc:1,vol:-1}},
{id:140052,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Postural & Spatial Dynamics",trait:"Stands at forty-five degrees",desc:"Never squares up to anyone, always a quarter turn off, in every conversation.",example:"<i>(addressing the wall a little to your left)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140053,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Postural & Spatial Dynamics",trait:"Takes the seat nearest the door",desc:"Chooses it invariably, without hurry, and appears unaware it is a choice.",example:"<i>(already sitting down before the room has been surveyed)</i>",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140054,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Postural & Spatial Dynamics",trait:"Leans back to agree",desc:"Withdraws physically at exactly the moments they are conceding a point.",example:"You're right. <i>(chair creaks backward)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{agr:1}},
{id:140055,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Gestural & Kinetic Integration",trait:"Gestures only with the left hand",desc:"The right stays entirely still throughout, whatever they are doing with the left.",example:"<i>(one hand drawing the shape of it, the other flat on the table)</i>",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140056,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Gestural & Kinetic Integration",trait:"Points with the chin",desc:"Never indicates with a hand; the direction always comes from a small lift of the jaw.",example:"<i>(chin toward the far door)</i> — that one.",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140057,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Vocal Modulation Mannerisms",trait:"Drops a tone to be serious",desc:"Signals gravity with pitch rather than volume, and the drop is small and unmistakable.",example:"<i>(half an octave down)</i> I need you to listen to this bit.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{vol:-1}},
{id:140058,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Vocal Modulation Mannerisms",trait:"Ends questions flat",desc:"No upward inflection ever, so every question sounds like a statement they've already answered.",example:"You're coming on Thursday.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{asrt:1}},
{id:140059,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Physical Vocalizations & Noises",trait:"One small breath before speaking",desc:"An audible intake precedes every utterance, including the very short ones.",example:"<i>(hh)</i> Yes. <i>(hh)</i> No.",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140060,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Physical Vocalizations & Noises",trait:"Clicks the tongue to think",desc:"A single soft click stands in for the pause where a filler would go.",example:"<i>(tk)</i> — probably Wednesday.",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140061,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Environmental Interaction Mannerisms",trait:"Reads whatever is nearest",desc:"Will silently read the label, spine or notice within reach while continuing the conversation perfectly.",example:"<i>(turning the jar to read the back of it)</i> — no, go on, I'm listening.",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{cur:1}},
{id:140062,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Environmental Interaction Mannerisms",trait:"Turns lights down on arrival",desc:"Adjusts the lighting in any room they will be in for more than a few minutes.",example:"<i>(dims the lamp two notches, sits)</i>",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140063,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Social & Boundary Mannerisms",trait:"Says the name back",desc:"Repeats a person's name once on being introduced, quietly, and then never gets it wrong.",example:"Priya. <i>(a beat)</i> Good to meet you, Priya.",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{man:1,warm:1}},
{id:140064,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Social & Boundary Mannerisms",trait:"Waits to be seated",desc:"Stands until told where to sit, in every setting, including informal ones.",example:"<i>(still standing, coat over the arm)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{man:1,asrt:-1}},
{id:140065,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Emotional Affectations",trait:"Apologises to objects",desc:"Says sorry, quietly and automatically, to furniture they bump into.",example:"<i>(knocks the chair)</i> — sorry.",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{man:1,ego:-1}},
{id:140066,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Emotional Affectations",trait:"Laughs at the wrong volume",desc:"The laugh is consistently either much smaller or much bigger than the joke, never matched.",example:"<i>(an enormous laugh at a very small remark)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140067,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Sartorial & Grooming Mannerisms",trait:"One item never changes",desc:"Everything else varies; a single garment or object is present in every memory anyone has of them.",example:"<i>(the same grey scarf, in July)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140068,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Sartorial & Grooming Mannerisms",trait:"Dressed for the previous decade",desc:"Immaculate and entirely coherent, just not from now, and not remarked upon.",example:"<i>(pressed, correct, and about fifteen years out)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},

/* ---------- Verbosity Traits ---------- */
{id:140069,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"Minimal & Ultra-Brief",trait:"Answers in the other person's words",desc:"Says as little as possible, and what little there is is borrowed from the question.",example:"\"Was it difficult?\" \"It was difficult.\"",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{vol:-1}},
{id:140070,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"Minimal & Ultra-Brief",trait:"Brief except about one thing",desc:"Four words for everything in the world and forty for a single subject.",example:"Fine. Fine. Yep. — Now, the drainage, that's actually interesting, because...",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{cur:1}},
{id:140071,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"Pacing & Situation-Driven",trait:"Slows down when angry",desc:"The pace drops rather than rises under provocation, and everyone learns to read it.",example:"I. See. Well. That's. Interesting.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{pace:-1,disc:1}},
{id:140072,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"Pacing & Situation-Driven",trait:"Pauses before agreeing, never before refusing",desc:"'No' is instant; 'yes' takes a considered beat, every time.",example:"No. — \"And Thursday?\" — <i>(pause)</i> — yes.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{disc:1}},
{id:140073,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"Stylized & Elaborate",trait:"One elaborate sentence per conversation",desc:"Plain throughout, and somewhere in every exchange produces a single carefully-built sentence.",example:"...anyway. It's the kind of quiet that has somebody else's footsteps in it.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140074,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"High-Volume & Wordy",trait:"Wordy only in writing",desc:"Terse in person and unstoppable the moment there is a keyboard between them and anyone.",example:"\"Fine.\" <i>(then a four-paragraph message at eleven that night)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{vol:1}},
{id:140075,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"Repetitive & Circular",trait:"Returns to one sentence",desc:"Circles a single formulation and comes back to it verbatim three or four times an hour.",example:"It's not that I mind. — ...anyway, it's not that I mind.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},

/* ---------- Personality Traits ---------- */
{id:140076,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Honesty — Truthful & Transparent",trait:"Volunteers the small correction",desc:"Cannot let an inaccurate detail stand even when it favours them and nobody would ever know.",example:"It was two years, not three. Sorry, it matters to me that it's right.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{hon:1}},
{id:140077,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Honesty — Deceptive & Evasive",trait:"Lies only about the trivial",desc:"Scrupulous on anything that matters and reflexively untruthful about things of no consequence.",example:"Yeah, I've read it. <i>(He has not, and it does not matter at all.)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{hon:-1}},
{id:140078,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Manners — Polished & Courteous",trait:"Courteous to the absent",desc:"Will not let a person be spoken badly of when they are not in the room, without making a speech about it.",example:"He's not here, though, is he. <i>(and moves the subject on)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{man:1,warm:1}},
{id:140079,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Manners — Crude & Ill-Mannered",trait:"Polite to strangers, coarse to intimates",desc:"Impeccable with anyone they'll never see again and entirely unfiltered with the people closest to them.",example:"Thank you so much. <i>(to the waiter)</i> — Move your bloody elbow. <i>(to his wife)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{man:-1,warm:-1}},
{id:140080,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Discipline — Self-Controlled",trait:"One rule, kept absolutely",desc:"Generally quite loose, and observes a single self-imposed rule with total consistency.",example:"I'll do most things. I don't drink before six. That one's not negotiable.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{disc:1}},
{id:140081,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Discipline — Impulsive & Undisciplined",trait:"Disciplined until observed",desc:"Keeps to the plan perfectly alone and abandons it the moment there is company.",example:"Been very good all week — go on then, one won't hurt.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{disc:-1,agr:1}},
{id:140082,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Cries at the wrong scene",desc:"Unmoved by the obviously sad thing and undone by something small and adjacent to it.",example:"<i>(dry through the funeral, gone at the sight of his coat on the hook)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:1}},
{id:140083,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Curiosity — Inquisitive & Exploratory",trait:"Asks the second question",desc:"Never satisfied with the first answer, always asks one more, and then stops.",example:"How long have you done it? — And what were you doing before that?",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{cur:1}},
{id:140084,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Curiosity — Incurious & Settled",trait:"Content with the first answer",desc:"Accepts explanations completely and has no impulse whatever to check them.",example:"Right, that makes sense. <i>(and it is genuinely finished)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{cur:-1}},
{id:140085,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Positivity — Pessimistic & Cynical",trait:"Expects the worst, quietly prepares for it",desc:"Says nothing gloomy out loud and has already packed for the disaster.",example:"Should be lovely. <i>(There are three days of water in the boot.)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{pos:-1,disc:1}},
{id:140086,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Assertiveness — Passive & Yielding",trait:"Concedes early to win late",desc:"Gives way on everything small so early that nobody notices they never give way on the thing that matters.",example:"Fine, fine, whatever you like. — No, not that. That one's mine.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{asrt:-1,intel:1}},
{id:140087,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Agreeableness — Accommodating",trait:"Assents sincerely, proceeds independently",desc:"Genuine, uncalculated assent in the room, followed by entirely independent action.",example:"Yes, absolutely. <i>(and then does the opposite, without any sense of having lied)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{agr:1,rebel:1}},
{id:140088,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Friendliness — Warm & Approachable",trait:"Warm to the overlooked",desc:"Ordinary with most people and unmistakably kind to whoever the room is ignoring.",example:"<i>(turns the chair slightly toward the one person nobody has spoken to)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{warm:1}},
{id:140089,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Friendliness — Cold & Distant",trait:"Kind in action, cold in manner",desc:"Does the generous thing reliably and gives nothing away doing it.",example:"<i>(paid the bill an hour ago; will not be thanked for it)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{warm:-1,emo:-1}},
{id:140090,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Rebelliousness — Compliant & Conformist",trait:"Follows the rule others have dropped",desc:"Keeps observing a convention long after everyone else has quietly stopped.",example:"<i>(still filling in the form nobody reads)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{rebel:-1,disc:1}},
{id:140091,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Right without a route",desc:"Arrives at the correct answer reliably and has never once been able to show the working.",example:"It's the second one. — Don't ask me why, it just is.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140092,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Unbothered by being wrong",desc:"Concedes errors instantly and cheerfully, with no visible cost.",example:"Oh, I'm completely wrong. Good. Carry on.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{ego:1,hon:1}},
{id:140093,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Activeness — Sedentary & Low-Energy",trait:"Still, then suddenly not",desc:"Motionless for very long stretches and then briefly, efficiently, fast.",example:"<i>(has not moved in forty minutes; crosses the room in four seconds)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{act:-1}},

/* ---------- Profile sections ---------- */
{id:140094,section:"Social Role in a Group",category:"Outsider",trait:"Invited everywhere, close to no one",desc:"Perfectly integrated on the surface and structurally outside it, which nobody has noticed including them.",example:"Everyone knows him. Ask any of them for his phone number.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{warm:-1}},
{id:140095,section:"Social Role in a Group",category:"Connector",trait:"Introduces people and leaves",desc:"Puts two people together, gives them one shared fact, and removes themselves.",example:"You two should talk about the canal thing. <i>(gone)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{warm:1}},
{id:140096,section:"Social Role in a Group",category:"Skeptic",trait:"Believes it, checks anyway",desc:"Not remotely suspicious, and verifies everything as a matter of habit.",example:"No, I'm sure you're right. I'll just have a look.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{intel:1}},
{id:140097,section:"Values & Moral Line",category:"Pragmatic & Flexible",trait:"Flexible except on time",desc:"Will bend on principle, money, and method, and not by five minutes on an agreed hour.",example:"Whatever works. Half seven means half seven, though.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{disc:1}},
{id:140098,section:"Values & Moral Line",category:"Loyalty-Bound",trait:"Loyal to a version that's gone",desc:"Keeps faith with who someone used to be, quietly, long past the evidence.",example:"He wasn't always like this. <i>(and that is enough)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{warm:1}},
{id:140099,section:"Attachment & Intimacy Style",category:"Secure",trait:"Says the awkward thing early",desc:"Raises small discomforts while they are still small, without drama, as a matter of course.",example:"That landed badly and I want to sort it out now rather than Thursday.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:1,hon:1}},
{id:140100,section:"Attachment & Intimacy Style",category:"Avoidant",trait:"Closest at a distance",desc:"Warm, open and generous in letters and on the phone, and unreachable in the same room.",example:"<i>(three pages, handwritten. Then twenty minutes of weather at the door.)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140101,section:"Attachment & Intimacy Style",category:"Anxious",trait:"Rereads sent messages",desc:"Goes back over what they already sent rather than waiting for the reply.",example:"<i>(scrolling up to check the tone of something written forty minutes ago)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{ego:-1}},
{id:140102,section:"Humor Style",category:"Dry & Deadpan",trait:"Never signals the joke",desc:"Delivers it identically to everything else and lets it land or not.",example:"Yes, I've always wanted to be buried at sea. In Rutland.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140103,section:"Humor Style",category:"Self-Deprecating",trait:"Undercuts only their competence",desc:"Cheerfully dismissive about what they're actually good at, and quietly proud of something trivial.",example:"Oh, anyone could do that. — I do make an excellent boiled egg.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{ego:-1}},
{id:140104,section:"Habits & Vices",category:"Restraint & Discipline",trait:"Abstains without announcing it",desc:"Simply doesn't, and has never once explained why, and deflects if asked.",example:"Not for me, thanks. — <i>(the subject is closed and nobody quite knows how)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{disc:1,emo:-1}},
{id:140105,section:"Habits & Vices",category:"Avoidance & Procrastination",trait:"Does the second-most urgent thing",desc:"Always productive, never on the actual item, and the substitution is invisible from outside.",example:"<i>(reorganised the entire filing system. The letter is still unopened.)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{disc:-1}},
{id:140106,section:"Conflict & Stress Response",category:"Freeze (shut down)",trait:"Keeps talking, stops being there",desc:"Speech continues perfectly fluently while the person behind it has left.",example:"Yes. Yes, that's right. Yes. <i>(nothing is going in)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140107,section:"Conflict & Stress Response",category:"Fawn (appease the threat)",trait:"Agrees faster the angrier they get",desc:"Their own rising fury expresses itself as accelerating agreement.",example:"Yes. Yep. Absolutely. You're right. Completely right. <i>(white-knuckled)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{agr:1,asrt:-1}},
{id:140108,section:"Conflict & Stress Response",category:"Flight (remove yourself)",trait:"Makes tea to leave the room",desc:"Has a repertoire of small errands that are all, in fact, exits.",example:"I'll put the kettle on. <i>(nobody asked for tea)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140109,section:"Motivation & Wound",category:"Core Want (conscious goal)",trait:"To finish one specific thing",desc:"The whole ambition is a single unfinished object, and they rarely mention it.",example:"There's a boat in my father's garage. It's been there nineteen years.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{disc:1}},
{id:140110,section:"Motivation & Wound",category:"The Lie They Believe",trait:"That they are the reasonable one",desc:"A quiet, total certainty that of everyone involved, they are the one behaving sensibly.",example:"I'm not saying anyone's at fault. I'm just the only one being realistic.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140111,section:"Motivation & Wound",category:"Core Fear (what they flee)",trait:"Being found ordinary",desc:"Not failure — mediocrity, specifically, and being seen to be it.",example:"It's fine. It's fine work. That's the problem, it's fine.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{ego:-1}},
{id:140112,section:"Appearance",category:"Presence — Unremarkable",trait:"Recognised only in context",desc:"Entirely familiar behind the counter and completely unplaceable in the street.",example:"I know you. Sorry — I know you from somewhere.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140113,section:"Appearance",category:"Movement & Bearing",trait:"Arrives without being heard",desc:"Nothing stealthy about it; they are simply always already in the doorway.",example:"<i>(has been standing there for some time)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140114,section:"Appearance",category:"Distinguishing Marks",trait:"A ring-shaped pale band",desc:"The mark of something worn for many years and not there now.",example:"<i>(the fourth finger is a shade lighter than the rest of the hand)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140115,section:"Appearance",category:"Upkeep — Immaculate",trait:"Immaculate above the table",desc:"Everything visible in a seated conversation is perfect; nothing below it is.",example:"<i>(collar, cuffs, hands — and shoes that have not been touched in a year)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},

/* ================================================================
   2. QUIET DISTINCTIVE — noticeable, not loud (intensity 1-2)
   ================================================================ */

/* ---------- Vocabulary Traits ---------- */
{id:140120,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Register & Formality Spectrum",trait:"Softens with 'a bit'",desc:"Attaches a small qualifier to almost every adjective, which lowers the register of everything.",example:"It's a bit cold. He was a bit rude, actually.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{form:-1,asrt:-1}},
{id:140121,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Register & Formality Spectrum",trait:"Uses full names for institutions",desc:"Never abbreviates an organisation, however long the name and however well everyone knows it.",example:"I rang the Department for Work and Pensions again this morning.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{form:1}},
{id:140122,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Register & Formality Spectrum",trait:"Matches the room within a sentence",desc:"Adjusts register audibly and quickly to whoever last spoke.",example:"...utterly unacceptable — nah, it's rubbish, innit.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140123,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Precision & Specificity Level",trait:"Names the brand",desc:"Never says the generic noun when there is a specific product name available.",example:"Pass me the Stanley knife. Not the Stanley knife, the other Stanley knife.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140124,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Precision & Specificity Level",trait:"Rounds everything to five",desc:"All quantities arrive pre-rounded, and the rounding is never acknowledged.",example:"About fifteen people. Maybe twenty-five quid.",intensity:1,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140125,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Phonetic & Auditory Qualities",trait:"Trails off on the last word",desc:"Volume drops steadily across each sentence so the ending has to be guessed.",example:"I thought we might go on the Tuesday, if that's...",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{vol:-1,asrt:-1}},
{id:140126,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Phonetic & Auditory Qualities",trait:"Over-articulates consonants",desc:"Every ending is fully sounded, which reads as careful rather than loud.",example:"I wan-ted to ask abou-t the arrangemen-ts.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{form:1,disc:1}},
{id:140127,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Abstractness & Sensory Modality",trait:"Gives everything a texture",desc:"Reaches for tactile words for things that have no texture at all.",example:"It was a rough sort of meeting. Grainy.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140128,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Abstractness & Sensory Modality",trait:"Talks in floor plans",desc:"Explains relationships and situations spatially, as arrangements of things in a room.",example:"He's over here, and she's put herself right over there, and I'm in the doorway.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140129,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Semantic Density & Modifiers",trait:"Two adjectives, always",desc:"Never one, never three; every noun arrives with a matched pair.",example:"A small, cold room. A long, unhelpful conversation.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140130,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Semantic Density & Modifiers",trait:"Hedges the strong word",desc:"Reaches for a big word and immediately files it down.",example:"It was a catastrophe. Well — not a catastrophe. A mess.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{asrt:-1}},
{id:140131,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Directness & Literalness",trait:"Says what they are about to say",desc:"Announces the shape of the sentence before producing it.",example:"I'm going to be blunt. — I don't want to go.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{hon:1,asrt:1}},
{id:140132,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Directness & Literalness",trait:"Refuses the euphemism",desc:"Substitutes the plain word for the soft one, without heat, every time.",example:"He didn't pass. He died.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{hon:1,man:-1}},
{id:140133,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Pragmatic Focus & Speech Functions",trait:"Ends on an instruction",desc:"However the exchange went, the last thing out of their mouth is something for you to do.",example:"...anyway. Ring me Thursday.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{asrt:1}},
{id:140134,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Pragmatic Focus & Speech Functions",trait:"Checks you're still there",desc:"Punctuates with small verifications that the listener is following.",example:"You with me? Right. So then —",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140135,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Morphological & Structural Lexicon",trait:"Compounds on the spot",desc:"Builds new hyphenated words as needed and uses them as though they were standard.",example:"It's a whole Tuesday-afternoon-shaped problem.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{cur:1}},
{id:140136,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Morphological & Structural Lexicon",trait:"Prefers the noun form",desc:"Nominalises reflexively, which flattens the energy out of everything.",example:"There was a discussion. There has been a deterioration.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:-1,form:1}},
{id:140137,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Conceptual Framework & Loanwords",trait:"Explains the etymology",desc:"Offers the root of a word unprompted, briefly, and moves on.",example:"Salary — from salt, they paid them in it. Anyway.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1,cur:1}},
{id:140138,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Conceptual Framework & Loanwords",trait:"Frames everything as a system",desc:"Reaches for structural vocabulary regardless of the subject.",example:"There's an input problem here, is what there is.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1,emo:-1}},
{id:140139,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Temporal Orientation & Tense Usage",trait:"Everything was 'the other day'",desc:"All past events collapse to the same vague recent distance regardless of when they were.",example:"I saw him the other day. <i>(It was 2014.)</i>",intensity:1,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140140,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Temporal Orientation & Tense Usage",trait:"Narrates in the future perfect",desc:"Describes the present in terms of how it will look later.",example:"This'll have been the week it turned, I expect.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140141,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Affective & Emotional Intensity",trait:"Reports feelings as facts",desc:"States emotional content flatly, as data, with no colour on it at all.",example:"I was frightened. That's all. Next thing.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:-1,hon:1}},
{id:140142,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Affective & Emotional Intensity",trait:"Borrows others' feelings first",desc:"Reaches the room's emotion before their own, and reports it as theirs.",example:"Everyone's a bit shaken, I think. — I am, I mean. I'm shaken.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:1,agr:1}},

/* ---------- Dialogue Grammar Traits ---------- */
{id:140143,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Anchors & Fillers",trait:"Opens with 'So'",desc:"Every contribution, including the first one, begins as though continuing something.",example:"So the thing about Thursday is —",intensity:1,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140144,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Anchors & Fillers",trait:"'Sorry' as punctuation",desc:"Apologises so frequently that it has stopped meaning anything, including to them.",example:"Sorry, could I — sorry — just the one thing, sorry.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{ego:-1,man:1}},
{id:140145,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Anchors & Fillers",trait:"Closes with 'anyway'",desc:"Uses it to end topics rather than to change them, which quietly forecloses the subject.",example:"...but there we are. Anyway.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140146,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Disfluencies & Flow",trait:"Breathes mid-clause",desc:"The pauses fall in structurally odd places, so the rhythm is subtly wrong.",example:"I told him that the — money was already — spent.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140147,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Disfluencies & Flow",trait:"Fluent until interrupted",desc:"Perfectly smooth alone and cannot recover the thread once broken into.",example:"— sorry, what was I — no, it's gone.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{asrt:-1}},
{id:140148,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Spoken Compression",trait:"Drops articles under pressure",desc:"Grammar sheds its small words first when they're rushed, and only then.",example:"Get car. Bring bag. Now.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{pace:1}},
{id:140149,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Spoken Compression",trait:"Answers in fragments",desc:"Never a full sentence in reply, always the operative piece of one.",example:"\"Where were you?\" \"Kitchen.\"",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{vol:-1}},
{id:140150,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Structural Shifts",trait:"Front-loads the condition",desc:"Every sentence puts the caveat first and the point last.",example:"If the weather holds and if the car starts, we'll come.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{asrt:-1}},
{id:140151,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Structural Shifts",trait:"Adds a clause after the full stop",desc:"Finishes, stops, then attaches a trailing fragment as a separate sentence.",example:"We're not going. Because of the money.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140152,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Turn-Taking Grammar",trait:"Overlaps only to agree",desc:"Speaks over people exclusively to confirm what they're saying, never to argue.",example:"— yes — yes — exactly that —",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{agr:1,warm:1}},
{id:140153,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Turn-Taking Grammar",trait:"Leaves a full beat before replying",desc:"A consistent, slightly-too-long gap that makes everyone else fill it.",example:"\"...well?\" <i>(two full seconds)</i> \"No.\"",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{pace:-1,asrt:1}},
{id:140154,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Repetition & Echo Patterns",trait:"Says it twice, differently",desc:"Restates every point immediately in other words, as though the first attempt failed.",example:"It's not viable. It won't work.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{vol:1}},
{id:140155,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Repetition & Echo Patterns",trait:"Repeats the word they dislike",desc:"Isolates and returns the one term in your sentence they object to.",example:"\"It's a compromise.\" \"Compromise.\"",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{agr:-1}},

/* ---------- Mannerisms ---------- */
{id:140156,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Micro-Physical Tics",trait:"Presses the thumb into the palm",desc:"A small self-contained pressure that runs whenever they are being spoken to.",example:"<i>(thumb working slowly into the opposite palm, under the table)</i>",intensity:1,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140157,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Micro-Physical Tics",trait:"Rolls the shoulder before speaking",desc:"One shoulder resets, small and habitual, at the start of every contribution.",example:"<i>(shoulder rolls back)</i> — the thing is —",intensity:1,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140158,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Eye & Facial Expressions",trait:"Eyebrows do the punctuation",desc:"Face stays otherwise still and the brows carry the entire emotional line.",example:"<i>(a small lift on 'apparently')</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140159,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Eye & Facial Expressions",trait:"Looks away to remember, back to speak",desc:"A reliable two-phase gaze that makes recall visible.",example:"<i>(off to the window)</i> — it was March. <i>(back)</i> — March.",intensity:1,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140160,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Tactile & Prop Handling",trait:"Peels labels",desc:"Systematically removes any label within reach, entire, and keeps the piece.",example:"<i>(the bottle is bare; the label is folded into eighths)</i>",intensity:1,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140161,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Tactile & Prop Handling",trait:"Stacks what's in front of them",desc:"Any loose items become an ordered pile within a minute of sitting down.",example:"<i>(coasters squared, phone aligned to the table edge)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{disc:1}},
{id:140162,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Postural & Spatial Dynamics",trait:"Sits on the front edge",desc:"Never settles back into a chair, in any setting, however long they're there.",example:"<i>(perched, feet flat, three hours in)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{act:1}},
{id:140163,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Postural & Spatial Dynamics",trait:"Keeps a hand on the doorframe",desc:"Enters rooms only partly, maintaining contact with the way out.",example:"<i>(half in, fingers still on the frame)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140164,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Gestural & Kinetic Integration",trait:"Draws the shape of it",desc:"Sketches structures in the air with a flat hand while explaining anything.",example:"<i>(a flat palm laying out three levels in the space between you)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1}},
{id:140165,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Gestural & Kinetic Integration",trait:"Counts on the fingers, visibly",desc:"Enumerates with the hand held up whether or not anyone needs the count.",example:"One, the money. <i>(thumb)</i> Two, the time. <i>(finger)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140166,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Vocal Modulation Mannerisms",trait:"Speeds up at the end",desc:"Every sentence accelerates through its final third, as though running out of permission.",example:"I thought we might — well I thoughtwemightgoonTuesday.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{pace:1,asrt:-1}},
{id:140167,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Vocal Modulation Mannerisms",trait:"Quiets to make you lean in",desc:"Drops volume rather than raising it when they want the room, and it works.",example:"<i>(barely audible)</i> — I wouldn't do that.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{vol:-1,asrt:1}},
{id:140168,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Physical Vocalizations & Noises",trait:"Sighs at the start, not the end",desc:"The exhale comes before the sentence, so it reads as preparation rather than exasperation.",example:"<i>(hhh)</i> — right, let's have a look.",intensity:1,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140169,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Physical Vocalizations & Noises",trait:"Small approving noise",desc:"A short 'mm' of assent that arrives at every acceptable thing, including objects.",example:"<i>(inspecting a chair)</i> Mm.",intensity:1,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{warm:1}},
{id:140170,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Environmental Interaction Mannerisms",trait:"Opens windows",desc:"Adjusts the air in any room within a few minutes, in any weather, without asking.",example:"<i>(the sash goes up four inches; it is February)</i>",intensity:1,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140171,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Environmental Interaction Mannerisms",trait:"Tests the exits",desc:"Locates the ways out of an unfamiliar room within the first minute, unhurriedly.",example:"<i>(a glance at the far door, then the window, then the conversation)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140172,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Social & Boundary Mannerisms",trait:"Fills other people's glasses",desc:"Attends to everyone's drink except their own, continuously.",example:"<i>(reaching for the jug before anyone has noticed they're low)</i>",intensity:1,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{warm:1}},
{id:140173,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Social & Boundary Mannerisms",trait:"Never sits with their back to a room",desc:"Rearranges seating quietly and firmly to keep the door in view.",example:"Do you mind if I take that one? — thanks.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140174,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Emotional Affectations",trait:"Deflects thanks with information",desc:"Answers gratitude with a logistical fact rather than acknowledging it.",example:"\"Thank you.\" \"It's in the second drawer if you need more.\"",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140175,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Emotional Affectations",trait:"Brightens on bad news",desc:"Voice and posture lift when something goes wrong, reliably and without irony.",example:"Oh — right! Well. That's that sorted, then, isn't it.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{pos:1,emo:-1}},
{id:140176,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Sartorial & Grooming Mannerisms",trait:"Dresses one degree too formally",desc:"Consistently a notch above the room, never enough to comment on.",example:"<i>(a jacket, at a barbecue)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{form:1}},
{id:140177,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Nods on the wrong beat",desc:"Encouraging and slightly out of time with what's being said.",example:"<i>(nodding steadily through a question)</i>",intensity:1,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},

/* ---------- Verbosity ---------- */
{id:140178,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"Minimal & Ultra-Brief",trait:"Lets the silence do it",desc:"Says nothing where a sentence was expected and simply waits.",example:"\"So what do you think?\" <i>(nothing)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{vol:-1,asrt:1}},
{id:140179,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"Pacing & Situation-Driven",trait:"Front-loads, then stops",desc:"Says the whole thing in the first ten seconds and has nothing further.",example:"He's not coming, the money's gone, and I'm going home. — That's it.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{pace:1}},
{id:140180,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"Stylized & Elaborate",trait:"Builds to the small point",desc:"Constructs elaborate approaches to conclusions of no importance.",example:"...and so, having considered all of that — I think I'll have the soup.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140181,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"High-Volume & Wordy",trait:"Talks through the decision",desc:"Thinks out loud at length and reaches the answer in public.",example:"So either we — no, because of Thursday — unless — right, no, Thursday's fine.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{vol:1,cur:1}},
{id:140182,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"Repetitive & Circular",trait:"Restates the question",desc:"Every answer begins by saying the question back, at slightly greater length.",example:"Am I worried about the money. Is that the question. About the money.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},

/* ---------- Personality & profile ---------- */
{id:140183,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Agreeableness — Contrarian & Argumentative",trait:"Argues the side they don't hold",desc:"Takes up the opposite position reflexively, cheerfully, and without conviction.",example:"I don't even think that. I just think somebody should say it.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{agr:-1,cur:1}},
{id:140184,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Pre-apologises for the work",desc:"Announces the flaws in what they've made before anyone can see it.",example:"It's rough. It's really rough. Don't look at the middle bit.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{ego:-1}},
{id:140185,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Answers feelings with logistics",desc:"Redirects any emotional question to a practical one, immediately and every time.",example:"\"How are you?\" \"The train was fine, actually, no delays.\"",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140186,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Finds the exception first",desc:"Reaches for the case that breaks the rule before engaging with the rule.",example:"Right — except for Tuesdays. What happens on Tuesdays?",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1}},
{id:140187,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Rebelliousness — Defiant",trait:"Reads the rule to find the gap",desc:"Complies exactly, having first located precisely how much compliance is required.",example:"It says by Friday. It doesn't say which Friday.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{rebel:1,intel:1}},
{id:140188,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Positivity — Optimistic & Upbeat",trait:"Finds the one good detail",desc:"Locates something genuinely worth having in every situation, however small.",example:"Well, the light in there was lovely.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{pos:1}},
{id:140189,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Activeness — Energetic & Active",trait:"Talks better walking",desc:"Noticeably more articulate in motion and stalls when made to sit.",example:"Can we do this on the way? I think better on the way.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{act:1}},
{id:140190,section:"Social Role in a Group",category:"Peacemaker",trait:"Names the agreement",desc:"Interrupts a disagreement to state the part both sides already accept.",example:"You both want it finished by Friday. Start there.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{agr:1,intel:1}},
{id:140191,section:"Social Role in a Group",category:"Leader",trait:"Decides by asking one person",desc:"Consults exactly one other person, always, and then commits publicly.",example:"Sam? — Right. We're doing it.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{asrt:1}},
{id:140192,section:"Social Role in a Group",category:"Instigator",trait:"Asks the question nobody will",desc:"Puts the awkward thing in the room, mildly, and lets it sit.",example:"Are we going to talk about the money, or not?",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{hon:1,man:-1}},
{id:140193,section:"Social Role in a Group",category:"Caretaker",trait:"Notices before they're asked",desc:"Acts on small needs a step ahead of anyone voicing them.",example:"<i>(the cardigan is already over the back of her chair)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{warm:1}},
{id:140194,section:"Values & Moral Line",category:"Rigid & Principled",trait:"Same rule for themselves",desc:"Applies their standard to their own conduct first, without announcing it.",example:"I said no phones at the table. That includes mine. <i>(puts it away)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{hon:1,disc:1}},
{id:140195,section:"Values & Moral Line",category:"Self-Interested",trait:"Helps where it's cheap",desc:"Reliably generous with anything that costs them nothing and immovable past that line.",example:"Course, take the car. — No, I can't lend you that.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140196,section:"Values & Moral Line",category:"Idealistic & Visionary",trait:"Talks about it as already done",desc:"Describes the thing they hope for in the past tense, as accomplished.",example:"When we sorted the water out, everything else got easier.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{pos:1}},
{id:140197,section:"Attachment & Intimacy Style",category:"Disorganized",trait:"Asks to be left, then follows",desc:"Requests distance sincerely and closes it again within the hour.",example:"Just go. — <i>(twenty minutes later)</i> — where did you go?",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:1}},
{id:140198,section:"Humor Style",category:"Warm & Playful",trait:"Jokes to include, not to land",desc:"The joke is a door held open rather than a performance.",example:"You've got the same face as him. Both of you. Terrible.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{warm:1}},
{id:140199,section:"Humor Style",category:"Intellectual & Wordplay",trait:"Amuses themselves audibly",desc:"Makes a small private joke, laughs at it alone, and does not explain.",example:"<i>(a short laugh at nothing anyone else can see)</i> — sorry, go on.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140200,section:"Humor Style",category:"Humorless & Absent",trait:"Answers the joke",desc:"Takes the literal content seriously and responds to it, without hostility.",example:"\"I could murder a pint.\" \"There's a place on the corner.\"",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140201,section:"Habits & Vices",category:"Compulsion & Ritual",trait:"Same route, always",desc:"Takes one path through a familiar journey and is visibly unsettled by a diversion.",example:"They've shut the bridge. — <i>(a long pause)</i> — right.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{disc:1}},
{id:140202,section:"Habits & Vices",category:"Substance & Consumption",trait:"Keeps count out loud",desc:"Announces each one as it happens, which is its own kind of permission.",example:"That's two. — That's three, then.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140203,section:"Habits & Vices",category:"Risk & Escape",trait:"Books things they may not attend",desc:"Buys the ticket to have the option, and often doesn't go.",example:"<i>(a ferry booking for Thursday that nobody has been told about)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140204,section:"Conflict & Stress Response",category:"Fight (attack the threat)",trait:"Gets very polite",desc:"Manners sharpen rather than fail under provocation, and everyone knows what it means.",example:"I'm terribly sorry — would you mind saying that again?",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{man:1,asrt:1}},
{id:140205,section:"Motivation & Wound",category:"Core Wound (the old injury)",trait:"Was told they were the easy one",desc:"Praised for needing nothing, at an age when they needed a great deal.",example:"Mum always said, thank God for you, you were never any trouble.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140206,section:"Motivation & Wound",category:"The Need (what would actually help)",trait:"To be allowed to do it badly",desc:"Needs one arena where the standard is off, and has never had one.",example:"I'd like to make something that doesn't have to be any good.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{disc:-1}},
{id:140207,section:"Appearance",category:"Build — Slight",trait:"Takes up less room than they have",desc:"Occupies a fraction of whatever space they are given, habitually.",example:"<i>(one third of a two-seater, coat on the lap)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140208,section:"Appearance",category:"Build — Imposing",trait:"Has to duck without thinking",desc:"Automatically adjusts for doorways and low beams, everywhere, unconsciously.",example:"<i>(head dips a fraction, three inches of clearance to spare)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140209,section:"Appearance",category:"Upkeep — Unkempt",trait:"Clean and disordered",desc:"Nothing dirty and nothing where it should be.",example:"<i>(fresh shirt, done up one button out)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{disc:-1}},
{id:140210,section:"Appearance",category:"Presence — Striking",trait:"Photographs differently",desc:"Doesn't stand out in a room and is unmistakable in every picture.",example:"That's never you. — It is, though.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},

/* ================================================================
   3. LOUD COMMON — big, unmissable, and entirely ordinary (i4-i5)
   ================================================================ */

{id:140220,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"High-Volume & Wordy",trait:"Tells the same story at every gathering",desc:"One anecdote, fully formed, deployed at length whenever there is a new listener.",example:"Did I ever tell you about the caravan? Right, so —",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1}},
{id:140221,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"High-Volume & Wordy",trait:"Answers a yes/no question for five minutes",desc:"Gives the full history whenever a single word would have done.",example:"\"Did you get the milk?\" \"Well, I went to the shop, and —\"",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1}},
{id:140222,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"High-Volume & Wordy",trait:"Keeps talking through the goodbye",desc:"Continues the conversation from the doorstep, the path, and the car window.",example:"— and the other thing, sorry — <i>(the engine is running)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1}},
{id:140223,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"High-Volume & Wordy",trait:"Explains the joke",desc:"Follows every joke with a full account of why it was funny.",example:"...because he'd said the same thing earlier, you see. That's the thing.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1}},
{id:140224,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"Repetitive & Circular",trait:"Says the same complaint every week",desc:"One grievance, reproduced almost word for word, indefinitely.",example:"And they still haven't done anything about that road.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{pos:-1}},
{id:140225,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"Minimal & Ultra-Brief",trait:"Grunts instead of answering",desc:"A one-syllable noise stands in for most replies, all day, to everyone.",example:"\"You alright?\" \"Nnh.\"",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:-1,warm:-1}},
{id:140226,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"Pacing & Situation-Driven",trait:"Talks over the film",desc:"Provides continuous commentary on anything anyone is trying to watch.",example:"He's the one from the other thing. He was in that. With the boat.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1}},
{id:140227,section:"Verbosity Traits",category:"Stylized & Elaborate",trait:"Quotes the same film constantly",desc:"Reaches for one source of lines relentlessly, regardless of the room.",example:"As they say — well, you know what they say.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{}},

{id:140228,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Affective & Emotional Intensity",trait:"Everything is 'literally' something",desc:"Uses a single intensifier constantly and at maximum, for everything.",example:"I was literally dying. It was literally the worst.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{emo:1}},
{id:140229,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Affective & Emotional Intensity",trait:"Swears as punctuation",desc:"Heavy, cheerful, entirely un-aimed profanity throughout.",example:"Bloody thing's bloody broken again, isn't it.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{man:-1,vol:1}},
{id:140230,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Register & Formality Spectrum",trait:"Talks to adults like children",desc:"Loud, slow, simplified speech applied indiscriminately.",example:"NOW. WE'RE GOING TO GO. IN THE CAR. ALRIGHT?",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{man:-1,vol:1}},
{id:140231,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Phonetic & Auditory Qualities",trait:"Simply very loud",desc:"No modulation, no awareness, the same volume in a library and a field.",example:"<i>(three tables away, entirely audible)</i>",intensity:5,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1}},
{id:140232,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Directness & Literalness",trait:"Says exactly what they think of your haircut",desc:"Unfiltered assessment offered promptly and without malice.",example:"Oh. You've had it cut. — No, it's fine. It's short.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{hon:1,man:-1}},
{id:140233,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Pragmatic Focus & Speech Functions",trait:"Turns every topic to their own",desc:"Whatever is being discussed becomes the same three subjects within a minute.",example:"Right, yeah — it's like when I was doing the extension —",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140234,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Precision & Specificity Level",trait:"Corrects everyone's grammar",desc:"Interrupts to fix usage, publicly, at any point in any conversation.",example:"Fewer. Fewer people. Not less.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{man:-1,intel:1}},
{id:140235,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Semantic Density & Modifiers",trait:"Absolutely everything is 'amazing'",desc:"One superlative, applied at full strength to a sandwich and to a bereavement.",example:"That's amazing. That's absolutely amazing.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{pos:1}},
{id:140236,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Conceptual Framework & Loanwords",trait:"Buries everything in workplace jargon",desc:"Corporate vocabulary applied relentlessly to domestic life.",example:"Let's circle back on the bins at the weekend.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{form:1}},
{id:140237,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Temporal Orientation & Tense Usage",trait:"Everything was better before",desc:"Constant, forceful comparison of the present to an earlier period.",example:"You couldn't have done that then. Wouldn't have been allowed.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{pos:-1}},
{id:140238,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Abstractness & Sensory Modality",trait:"Describes food in enormous detail",desc:"Full sensory accounts of every meal, to anyone, unprompted.",example:"...and the sauce, right, the sauce had a sort of a — a nuttiness.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1}},
{id:140239,section:"Vocabulary Traits",category:"Morphological & Structural Lexicon",trait:"Nicknames everyone immediately",desc:"Assigns a shortened form on first meeting and uses it forever.",example:"Alright, Big Man. — Sit down, Chief.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{warm:1,man:-1}},

{id:140240,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Turn-Taking Grammar",trait:"Finishes everyone's sentences",desc:"Supplies the ending constantly, confidently, and often wrongly.",example:"— to the shop? — no — to the —  \"To the hospital.\" \"Right, the shop.\"",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{asrt:1,man:-1}},
{id:140241,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Turn-Taking Grammar",trait:"Interrupts to say 'exactly'",desc:"Breaks in constantly to agree, at volume, before the point has landed.",example:"— exactly — exactly — that's exactly it —",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{agr:1,vol:1}},
{id:140242,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Anchors & Fillers",trait:"'D'you know what I mean' after everything",desc:"A verbal tic deployed several times per sentence, at full volume.",example:"It's mental, d'you know what I mean, absolutely mental, d'you know what I mean.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1}},
{id:140243,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Disfluencies & Flow",trait:"Loses the thread loudly",desc:"Abandons long sentences audibly, repeatedly, and starts again from the top.",example:"So the — no, hang on — right, so — no. Start again.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1}},
{id:140244,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Spoken Compression",trait:"Shouts single words across rooms",desc:"Conducts most household communication as isolated bellowed nouns.",example:"KEYS. — WHAT? — KEYS!",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1}},
{id:140245,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Structural Shifts",trait:"Starts three sentences at once",desc:"Runs several thoughts together at speed without finishing any of them.",example:"And the other thing is — because he never — which is why I said —",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{pace:1,vol:1}},
{id:140246,section:"Dialogue Grammar Traits",category:"Repetition & Echo Patterns",trait:"Repeats it until acknowledged",desc:"Says the same sentence at increasing volume until someone responds.",example:"I said the bin needs doing. The bin needs doing. THE BIN.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1,agr:-1}},

{id:140247,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Physical Vocalizations & Noises",trait:"Sighs so everyone hears it",desc:"A large, unmissable exhale deployed as a public communication.",example:"<i>(an enormous sigh, directed at nobody and at everybody)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1,agr:-1}},
{id:140248,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Physical Vocalizations & Noises",trait:"Groans standing up",desc:"Announces every transition between sitting and standing at volume.",example:"<i>(ohhhhh)</i> — right.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{act:-1}},
{id:140249,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Vocal Modulation Mannerisms",trait:"Laughs at their own jokes first",desc:"Begins laughing before the punchline arrives, loudly, every time.",example:"— and he said — <i>(already going)</i> — he said —",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1,ego:1}},
{id:140250,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Gestural & Kinetic Integration",trait:"Big arms when telling a story",desc:"Full-span gesturing that takes over whatever space is available.",example:"<i>(both arms out; the pint goes over)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{act:1,vol:1}},
{id:140251,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Postural & Spatial Dynamics",trait:"Stands far too close",desc:"Habitually within a foot of whoever they're addressing, unaware.",example:"<i>(everyone in the conversation has taken a step back twice)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{man:-1}},
{id:140252,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Social & Boundary Mannerisms",trait:"Hugs everyone on arrival",desc:"Full, extended, non-negotiable physical greeting for all present.",example:"<i>(already halfway across the room, arms out)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{warm:1,man:-1}},
{id:140253,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Emotional Affectations",trait:"Cries very easily and very visibly",desc:"Tears arrive readily and at length, over adverts as much as over grief.",example:"<i>(fully gone, at a building society commercial)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{emo:1}},
{id:140254,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Environmental Interaction Mannerisms",trait:"Turns the television up",desc:"Raises the volume steadily throughout the evening and denies doing it.",example:"I haven't touched it. <i>(it is at 42)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1}},
{id:140255,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Tactile & Prop Handling",trait:"Clicks a pen continuously",desc:"Loud, sustained, entirely unconscious, and impossible to ignore.",example:"<i>(click. click. click. click.)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{act:1}},
{id:140256,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Eye & Facial Expressions",trait:"Rolls their eyes at everything",desc:"A large, visible, frequently-deployed eye-roll, aimed at whoever is speaking.",example:"<i>(a full rotation, in plain view)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{agr:-1,man:-1}},
{id:140257,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Micro-Physical Tics",trait:"Jiggles the whole table",desc:"A relentless leg bounce that transmits to every object in contact with it.",example:"<i>(the glasses are moving)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{act:1}},
{id:140258,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Sartorial & Grooming Mannerisms",trait:"Wildly overdressed for everything",desc:"Consistently and unmissably formal for occasions that are not.",example:"<i>(dinner jacket. It is a pub quiz.)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{form:1}},
{id:140259,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Interrupts to check their phone",desc:"Breaks eye contact and conversation to look at a screen, repeatedly and openly.",example:"Sorry — yeah — <i>(looking down)</i> — no, go on.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{man:-1,cur:-1}},

{id:140260,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Agreeableness — Contrarian & Argumentative",trait:"Argues about the route",desc:"Contests the way to anywhere, loudly, every journey.",example:"You don't want to go that way. You never want to go that way.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{agr:-1,vol:1}},
{id:140261,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Fishes for compliments constantly",desc:"Runs down their own work at volume until someone contradicts it.",example:"It's terrible, isn't it. It's terrible. — No, go on, say it's terrible.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:-1,vol:1}},
{id:140262,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Positivity — Pessimistic & Cynical",trait:"Predicts disaster out loud",desc:"Announces the worst outcome for every plan, in detail, in advance.",example:"It'll rain. It'll rain and the whole thing will be a washout.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{pos:-1,vol:1}},
{id:140263,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Manners — Crude & Ill-Mannered",trait:"Eats with their mouth open",desc:"Loud, unselfconscious, and entirely unresponsive to being told.",example:"<i>(audible from the next room)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{man:-1}},
{id:140264,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Activeness — Energetic & Active",trait:"Cannot sit through a meal",desc:"Up and down repeatedly throughout, always fetching something.",example:"<i>(fourth time out of the chair; nobody wanted more bread)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{act:1}},
{id:140265,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Discipline — Impulsive & Undisciplined",trait:"Buys things on the way home",desc:"Arrives with large unplanned purchases, frequently and cheerfully.",example:"I know. I know. But look at it.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{disc:-1}},
{id:140266,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Friendliness — Warm & Approachable",trait:"Talks to everyone in the queue",desc:"Strikes up full conversations with strangers everywhere, at length.",example:"<i>(now knows the cashier's daughter's exam results)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{warm:1,vol:1}},
{id:140267,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Friendliness — Cold & Distant",trait:"Leaves without saying goodbye",desc:"Simply goes, from every gathering, with no acknowledgement at all.",example:"<i>(the coat is gone; nobody saw)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{warm:-1,man:-1}},
{id:140268,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Assertiveness — Assertive & Direct",trait:"Sends the food back",desc:"Complains promptly and audibly in restaurants, always.",example:"No. No, this is cold. Take it back.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{asrt:1,man:-1}},
{id:140269,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Assertiveness — Passive & Yielding",trait:"Never picks the restaurant",desc:"Defers every choice, at length, until someone else is forced to decide.",example:"I don't mind. Honestly. Anywhere. You choose. I really don't mind.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{asrt:-1}},
{id:140270,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Honesty — Deceptive & Evasive",trait:"Says they're five minutes away",desc:"A reflexive, unvarying lie about their location, every time, to everyone.",example:"Just coming round the corner now. <i>(has not left)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{hon:-1}},
{id:140271,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Curiosity — Inquisitive & Exploratory",trait:"Asks strangers personal questions",desc:"Goes straight past small talk to the interesting thing, loudly, on no acquaintance.",example:"So why did you leave, then? Was it money?",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{cur:1,man:-1}},
{id:140272,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Rebelliousness — Defiant",trait:"Ignores signs on principle",desc:"Visibly and consistently disregards posted instructions, and says so.",example:"<i>(walks straight past 'Staff Only')</i> They can ask me to leave.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{rebel:1}},
{id:140273,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Rebelliousness — Compliant & Conformist",trait:"Asks permission for everything",desc:"Loudly checks before every action, however small, in every setting.",example:"Is it alright if I — sorry — is it alright if I sit here?",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{rebel:-1,asrt:-1}},
{id:140274,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Refuses to read instructions",desc:"Starts assembling immediately, loudly, and rejects the manual on principle.",example:"I don't need it. I can see how it goes.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{intel:-1,rebel:1}},
{id:140275,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Tells everyone everything immediately",desc:"Full emotional disclosure to near-strangers within minutes.",example:"Sorry — we've just met — but honestly, this year has been so hard.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{emo:1,vol:1}},
{id:140276,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Changes the subject loudly",desc:"Cuts across any emotional turn with a large, obvious topic change.",example:"ANYWAY. Has anyone seen the football?",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{emo:-1,vol:1}},
{id:140277,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Discipline — Self-Controlled",trait:"Announces the schedule",desc:"States the plan and the timings, at volume, repeatedly, to everyone.",example:"Right. Leaving at eight. Eight. Not five past.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{disc:1,vol:1}},
{id:140278,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Manners — Polished & Courteous",trait:"Insists on paying, loudly",desc:"A prolonged, public, non-negotiable performance of picking up every bill.",example:"No. No. Put it away. Put it AWAY.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{man:1,vol:1}},
{id:140279,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Sings in public",desc:"Full voice, no self-consciousness, in shops and on pavements.",example:"<i>(entire chorus, in the frozen aisle)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:1,vol:1}},

{id:140280,section:"Conflict & Stress Response",category:"Fight (attack the threat)",trait:"Raises their voice immediately",desc:"Volume is the first response to any friction, without escalation in between.",example:"WHAT. What did you just say to me.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1,asrt:1}},
{id:140281,section:"Conflict & Stress Response",category:"Flight (remove yourself)",trait:"Walks out mid-argument",desc:"Physically leaves, loudly, whenever a disagreement passes a certain point.",example:"<i>(the front door)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{}},
{id:140282,section:"Conflict & Stress Response",category:"Freeze (shut down)",trait:"Goes completely silent for days",desc:"A total, unmissable withdrawal of speech, sustained well past the incident.",example:"<i>(four days. Nothing.)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:-1}},
{id:140283,section:"Conflict & Stress Response",category:"Fawn (appease the threat)",trait:"Apologises for other people",desc:"Loudly takes responsibility for things done by everyone in the room.",example:"That's my fault, that's my fault, I should have said.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:-1,agr:1}},
{id:140284,section:"Social Role in a Group",category:"Instigator",trait:"Winds people up for sport",desc:"Provokes reliably and openly, mostly for the entertainment of watching.",example:"Go on, ask him about the extension. <i>(sits back)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{agr:-1}},
{id:140285,section:"Social Role in a Group",category:"Leader",trait:"Organises everything, unasked",desc:"Assumes command of any group activity, at volume, without being invited to.",example:"Right — you two, chairs. You, drinks. I'll do the rest.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{asrt:1,disc:1}},
{id:140286,section:"Social Role in a Group",category:"Skeptic",trait:"Says 'well, actually' constantly",desc:"Interrupts to correct factual details, loudly, in every conversation.",example:"Well, actually, it was 1987.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{agr:-1,intel:1}},
{id:140287,section:"Habits & Vices",category:"Substance & Consumption",trait:"Always has a drink in hand",desc:"Visibly, continuously, from arrival to departure, at every occasion.",example:"<i>(the glass is never empty and never full)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{disc:-1}},
{id:140288,section:"Habits & Vices",category:"Avoidance & Procrastination",trait:"Leaves everything to the last night",desc:"An unmissable annual crisis, complained about loudly throughout.",example:"<i>(2am, the whole thing still to do, again)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{disc:-1}},
{id:140289,section:"Habits & Vices",category:"Compulsion & Ritual",trait:"Checks the door three times",desc:"An open, repeated, unhurried verification ritual before leaving anywhere.",example:"<i>(back down the path. Again.)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{disc:1}},
{id:140290,section:"Humor Style",category:"Cruel & Barbed",trait:"Makes jokes about people present",desc:"Loud, personal material aimed at whoever is in the room.",example:"He's not stupid, he just hasn't had an idea since 2009.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{warm:-1,man:-1}},
{id:140291,section:"Humor Style",category:"Absurd & Chaotic",trait:"Does voices",desc:"Performs impressions constantly, at volume, for everyone and no one.",example:"<i>(now doing the neighbour, badly, at length)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1}},
{id:140292,section:"Attachment & Intimacy Style",category:"Anxious",trait:"Rings repeatedly when unanswered",desc:"Escalates contact loudly and quickly when a message goes unreturned.",example:"<i>(six missed calls in eleven minutes)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{emo:1}},
{id:140293,section:"Attachment & Intimacy Style",category:"Avoidant",trait:"Says they're busy for weeks",desc:"A consistent, obvious, entirely unbelievable unavailability.",example:"Mad month. Let's do something in the spring.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140294,section:"Values & Moral Line",category:"Rigid & Principled",trait:"Lectures about it at dinner",desc:"Delivers the position at length, unprompted, to a captive table.",example:"And I'll tell you exactly what's wrong with that —",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1,agr:-1}},
{id:140295,section:"Values & Moral Line",category:"Pragmatic & Flexible",trait:"Openly ignores the rule",desc:"Announces which regulations they're disregarding and why, cheerfully.",example:"They say two per customer. I'm taking four.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{rebel:1}},
{id:140296,section:"Motivation & Wound",category:"Core Want (conscious goal)",trait:"Wants everyone at the table",desc:"An enormous, openly-stated, endlessly-organised wish for the family gathered.",example:"I just want us all in one room. Once. Is that so much?",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{warm:1,vol:1}},
{id:140297,section:"Motivation & Wound",category:"Core Fear (what they flee)",trait:"Terrified of being late",desc:"An unmissable, vocal, hours-early relationship with every appointment.",example:"We're going to be late. We're going to be LATE.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{disc:1}},
{id:140298,section:"Appearance",category:"Presence — Striking",trait:"Very brightly dressed",desc:"Visible across any room, at any distance, always.",example:"<i>(the coat is orange. It is always orange.)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{}},
{id:140299,section:"Appearance",category:"Movement & Bearing",trait:"Walks very fast",desc:"Everyone else is always half a step behind, everywhere.",example:"<i>(already at the corner)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{act:1}},
{id:140300,section:"Appearance",category:"Upkeep — Unkempt",trait:"Visibly slept in it",desc:"Unmissably crumpled, every day, without apology.",example:"<i>(same shirt, worse)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{disc:-1}},
{id:140301,section:"Appearance",category:"Build — Imposing",trait:"Fills the doorway",desc:"Physically dominates any entrance they stand in, without trying to.",example:"<i>(the light from the hall is gone)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{}},
{id:140302,section:"Appearance",category:"Distinguishing Marks",trait:"A large visible tattoo",desc:"Immediately and permanently noticeable, and never explained.",example:"<i>(from the wrist to the collar, on both sides)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{}},

/* ================================================================
   4. THE THIN VARIANT SIDES
   ----------------------------------------------------------------
   Egotistical 11 : Insecure 38, Shallow 12 : Guarded 37, Unanalytical
   11 : Instinctive 43. Written to be caught by the side-b regexes in
   PRESENTATION_VARIANTS rather than by loosening them, so the tagger
   keeps its precision and the pools stop being 3.5 : 1.
   ================================================================ */

/* ---------- Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical :: EGOTISTICAL ---------- */
{id:140310,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Grandiose about small wins",desc:"Vain, boastful framing applied to entirely ordinary accomplishments.",example:"I'd say I more or less carried that meeting, honestly.",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140311,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Credential-drops in the first minute",desc:"Arrogant establishment of standing before anyone has asked what they do.",example:"When I was running the northern operation — anyway, sorry, you were saying?",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140312,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Never admits fault, ever",desc:"Conceited to the point that an error is always relocated to someone else.",example:"I was given the wrong information. That's not the same as being wrong.",intensity:4,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{ego:1,hon:-1}},
{id:140313,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Preens at any mirror",desc:"Vain, unhurried self-inspection in every reflective surface they pass.",example:"<i>(a long look at the darkened window; a small adjustment)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140314,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Entitled to the better seat",desc:"Self-important assumption of the best chair, table and position, always.",example:"<i>(has already taken the one by the window)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:1,man:-1}},
{id:140315,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Superior about other people's taste",desc:"Smug, unmistakable condescension toward what everyone else likes.",example:"Oh, that's — no, that's lovely. For what it is.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{ego:1,warm:-1}},
{id:140316,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Name-drops in every anecdote",desc:"Boastful insertion of well-known names into stories that don't require them.",example:"...which is exactly what Fiona said to me, actually. Fiona Hartley.",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140317,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Attention-hungry in a quiet room",desc:"Visibly deflates without the spotlight and works audibly to recover it.",example:"<i>(a louder laugh, at nothing, to bring the table back)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{ego:1,vol:1}},
{id:140318,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Quietly certain they're the best there",desc:"Conceited without any display at all — the assumption simply never moves.",example:"<i>(says nothing; has already privately ranked the room)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140319,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Self-aggrandising about suffering",desc:"Grandiose framing of their own difficulties as uniquely severe.",example:"Nobody in this family has been through what I've been through.",intensity:4,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{ego:1,emo:1}},
{id:140320,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Magnificently unbothered by evidence",desc:"Arrogant imperviousness to being shown, plainly, that they are mistaken.",example:"Well, that's one interpretation of the figures.",intensity:4,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{ego:1,intel:-1}},
{id:140321,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Showy generosity",desc:"Vain, public giving, calibrated to be seen rather than to be useful.",example:"<i>(the largest note, held up a beat too long)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{ego:1,warm:1}},
{id:140322,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Peacock about a single skill",desc:"Boastful, repetitive display of one genuine competence, forever.",example:"I'll do it. I'm better at it. It's just true, isn't it.",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140323,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Admires their own phrasing",desc:"Conceited, audible pleasure in something they have just said.",example:"...a slow kind of leaving. <i>(a small pause)</i> That's rather good.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140324,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Entitled to be waited for",desc:"Self-important assumption that any group will hold for them.",example:"They'll wait. <i>(and does not hurry)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{ego:1,man:-1}},
{id:140325,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Grandiose plans, no first step",desc:"Vast, confidently-announced ambitions with nothing underneath them.",example:"By this time next year the whole thing'll be running.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:1,disc:-1}},
{id:140326,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Boastful about being humble",desc:"An arrogance that has found a way to present as modesty.",example:"I never talk about it, actually. That's not who I am.",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140327,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Smug when proved right",desc:"Vain, unhidden satisfaction at any vindication, however minor.",example:"I did say. I'm not going to labour it. But I did say.",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140328,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Never-wrong about directions",desc:"Arrogant certainty about routes, sustained past all evidence.",example:"It's this way. — It's this way.",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140329,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Superior about their own upbringing",desc:"Conceited comparisons of how they were raised to how everyone else was.",example:"We weren't allowed to behave like that. Different world.",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140330,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Spotlight-seeking at other people's events",desc:"Attention-hungry in exactly the settings that belong to someone else.",example:"<i>(the speech at the wedding is now about him)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{ego:1,man:-1}},
{id:140331,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Quietly vain about one feature",desc:"An entirely contained conceit, attached to a single physical detail.",example:"<i>(the hands are always visible, always arranged)</i>",intensity:1,rarity:"signature",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140332,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Self-important about their time",desc:"Grandiose accounting of their own availability as uniquely scarce.",example:"I've moved three things to be here.",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140333,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Braggart about money, obliquely",desc:"Boastful references to cost, framed as complaint.",example:"Don't ask what the roof cost. Honestly. Don't ask.",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140334,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Insecure or Egotistical",trait:"Conceited about their own restraint",desc:"Vain specifically about how much they are choosing not to say.",example:"There's a lot I could say here. I won't.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{ego:1,disc:1}},

/* ---------- Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow :: SHALLOW ---------- */
{id:140340,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Cannot locate the feeling",desc:"Alexithymic rather than withholding: asked what they feel, there is nothing there to report.",example:"I don't — I genuinely don't know. It's blank.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140341,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Flat through good news",desc:"Numb in both directions; the pleasant things land as quietly as the bad ones.",example:"Oh. Right. Good.",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{emo:-1,pos:-1}},
{id:140342,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Surface warmth, no interior",desc:"Entirely pleasant and entirely empty behind it, which takes years to notice.",example:"<i>(the right words, in the right order, from nowhere)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:-1,warm:1}},
{id:140343,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Feels it four days late",desc:"Feels things four days late, if at all, and by then the moment has gone.",example:"I think I was upset about that. Last week. I've only just noticed.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140344,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"One acceptable emotion",desc:"Everything routes through a single available feeling, usually mild irritation.",example:"<i>(grief, fear and love all arriving as mild annoyance about the parking)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140345,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"No access to the past",desc:"Hollow where the memory of feeling should be; the events are there, the weight isn't.",example:"I know it happened. I can't get at what it was like.",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140346,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Unfeeling about animals",desc:"A blank where almost everyone has something, and no awareness of the gap.",example:"It's a dog. <i>(genuinely puzzled by the room)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{emo:-1,warm:-1}},
{id:140347,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Copies the room's emotion",desc:"No remaining access to their own, so they read the room and reproduce it.",example:"<i>(checks three faces, then arranges their own to match)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:-1,agr:1}},
{id:140348,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Shallow about their own history",desc:"Recounts serious events with the affect of a train timetable.",example:"Then she left, and I moved to Leeds. Anyway, the flat was fine.",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140349,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Numb under pressure",desc:"Where others flood, nothing arrives at all, which reads as courage and isn't.",example:"<i>(perfectly steady, because there is nothing to steady)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140350,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Empty on the anniversary",desc:"Marks the date correctly and feels nothing on it, every year.",example:"It's today, isn't it. <i>(and that is all there is)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140351,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Blank at partings",desc:"Says goodbye to people they may not see again with nothing behind it.",example:"Right. Safe trip.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:-1,warm:-1}},
{id:140352,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Nothing there to hide",desc:"Reads as stoic, and there is in fact no withheld interior at all.",example:"People think I'm holding something back. I'm not.",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140353,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Void where the fear should be",desc:"An absent threat response that has never once been present.",example:"I've never actually been frightened of anything. Is that odd?",intensity:4,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140354,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Surface-level about everyone",desc:"Knows facts about people and has formed no attachment to any of them.",example:"Two kids, works in insurance. — No, I couldn't tell you what he's like.",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{emo:-1,warm:-1}},
{id:140355,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Flat affect in a crisis and after",desc:"Neither during nor afterwards; the whole event passes without registering.",example:"<i>(same voice at the hospital as at the shops)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140356,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Learned the words for it",desc:"Has assembled a working emotional vocabulary from observation, not experience.",example:"That must have been very hard for you. <i>(correct, and from a manual)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140357,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Empty after the argument",desc:"No residue at all once it's over, which the other person finds unbearable.",example:"I'm not upset. I was never upset. Are we eating?",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140358,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Numb to praise",desc:"Compliments land on nothing; they are heard and not felt.",example:"Thanks. <i>(and it has already gone)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{emo:-1,ego:-1}},
{id:140359,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"No interior monologue about people",desc:"Thinks constantly about problems and never once about how anyone feels.",example:"I hadn't considered it. It genuinely hadn't come up.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:-1,intel:1}},
{id:140360,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Hollow enthusiasm",desc:"Produces excitement on cue with nothing supplying it.",example:"That's great! That's really great. <i>(nothing moves behind it)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{emo:-1,pos:1}},
{id:140361,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Blank about their own children",desc:"Attends fully to the practicalities and reports no feeling underneath.",example:"They're fed, they're fine. — Feel? They're my children.",intensity:4,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140362,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Shallow grief, unhidden",desc:"Openly says the loss did not affect them much, without defensiveness.",example:"Everyone kept asking. I was alright. I was just alright.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:-1,hon:1}},
{id:140363,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Guarded & Shallow",trait:"Surface reaction, correct timing",desc:"Flinches, softens and comforts precisely on cue, from nowhere at all.",example:"<i>(the face does the right thing; nothing else does)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:-1}},

/* ---------- Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical :: UNANALYTICAL ---------- */
{id:140370,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Cannot follow a conditional",desc:"Loses the thread the moment a sentence contains 'if', and says so.",example:"If we — no. Say it again without the ifs.",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140371,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Overwhelmed by two options",desc:"A genuine limitation rather than indecision: a fork stalls them completely.",example:"Just tell me which one. Please. Just tell me.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:-1,asrt:-1}},
{id:140372,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Needs a concrete example every time",desc:"Abstractions do not land at all until they are given something to hold.",example:"Give us an actual one. A real one. Then I'll get it.",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140373,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Theory-impatient to a fault",desc:"Rejects any explanation of why, which costs them repeatedly.",example:"I don't need the background. Just tell me what to do.",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{intel:-1,cur:-1}},
{id:140374,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Unreflective about repeated mistakes",desc:"Makes the same error for years without ever standing back from it.",example:"Bad luck again. Terrible luck, me.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140375,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Naive about people's motives",desc:"Takes stated reasons entirely at face value, always, and is regularly caught.",example:"He said he'd forgotten. Why would he say it if it wasn't true?",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{intel:-1,hon:1}},
{id:140376,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Holds exactly one consideration",desc:"Cannot hold a second consideration alongside the first, and doesn't try.",example:"Do the door. Then I'll think about the window.",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140377,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Simple-minded about money",desc:"No model of it beyond what is currently in the account.",example:"There's money in there. So we're fine.",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{intel:-1,disc:-1}},
{id:140378,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Unanalytical about their own moods",desc:"Never once asked why a feeling arrived; it simply does and then goes.",example:"I'm in a mood. — No idea. Just am.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:-1,emo:-1}},
{id:140379,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Repeats the simple explanation",desc:"Has one account of a complicated thing and returns to it unchanged.",example:"It's greed. That's all it is. It's greed.",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140380,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Cannot follow written instructions",desc:"The words go in and nothing assembles; needs to be shown, every time.",example:"Just do it once while I watch.",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140381,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Naive about being liked",desc:"Assumes goodwill universally and has never once revised the assumption.",example:"No, he's lovely. Everyone's lovely, really.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:-1,warm:1}},
{id:140382,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Dull to implication",desc:"Hears only the literal content and misses every inference in it.",example:"\"It's getting late.\" \"Ten past nine.\"",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140383,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Overwhelmed by a form",desc:"Paperwork of any complexity stops them completely and is quietly avoided.",example:"<i>(the envelope has been on the side for five weeks)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:-1,disc:-1}},
{id:140384,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Simple-minded about consequences",desc:"The second step of anything is genuinely not visible from the first.",example:"I didn't think that'd happen. — How would I have known?",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140385,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Never once explained a decision",desc:"Cannot produce a reason for anything they have chosen, including large things.",example:"I just did. That's the whole of it.",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140386,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Unreflective about their own past",desc:"Recounts events without ever having connected any two of them.",example:"That was that. Then the other thing happened.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140387,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Cannot follow a map",desc:"The representation and the world do not connect, and never have.",example:"Which way up is it?",intensity:2,rarity:"common",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140388,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Naive about scale",desc:"No feel for magnitude, so a thousand and a million are the same word.",example:"It's a lot either way, isn't it.",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140389,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Simple-explanation-seeking under pressure",desc:"Reaches for the shortest available account precisely when it fits worst.",example:"Somebody must have moved it. That'll be it.",intensity:4,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140390,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Dimwitted about jokes at their expense",desc:"Joins in enthusiastically without registering the direction of them.",example:"<i>(laughing hardest, at himself, not knowing)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{intel:-1,warm:1}},
{id:140391,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Unanalytical loyalty",desc:"Backs a person absolutely with no examination of the position at all.",example:"He's my brother. That's the end of it.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{intel:-1,warm:1}},
{id:140392,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Overwhelmed by a changed plan",desc:"A revision to an agreed arrangement is genuinely, visibly, too much.",example:"But we said Tuesday. We said Tuesday.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:-1,disc:1}},
{id:140393,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Instinctive & Unanalytical",trait:"Never once been able to show the working",desc:"Reaches conclusions and has no route to them, correct or otherwise.",example:"Don't ask me how I got there. I just got there.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{intel:-1}},

/* ================================================================
   5. LISTENING & ATTENTION — the smallest category in the bank
   ----------------------------------------------------------------
   24 traits, no i1 and no i5, against Mannerism siblings at 74-79.
   ================================================================ */
{id:140400,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Hears the correction, not the point",desc:"Latches onto the one factual slip in a paragraph and loses the rest.",example:"— it was Wednesday, though, wasn't it? — sorry, carry on.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1,warm:-1}},
{id:140401,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Waits to speak",desc:"Visibly holding a prepared sentence throughout whatever you are saying.",example:"<i>(mouth already half open, three sentences ago)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{asrt:1,warm:-1}},
{id:140402,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Stops moving to listen",desc:"Everything else halts completely the moment something matters.",example:"<i>(the hands go still; the whole body arrives)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{warm:1}},
{id:140403,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Listens with their eyes closed",desc:"Shuts them to concentrate, which reads as disengagement and is the opposite.",example:"<i>(eyes closed, nodding slowly)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140404,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Only hears the first sentence",desc:"Attention closes as soon as they think they know where it's going.",example:"Right, yes, I know this one —",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{cur:-1}},
{id:140405,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Takes notes in conversation",desc:"Writes things down mid-exchange, in any setting, including social ones.",example:"<i>(a small pad; the date and three words)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{disc:1}},
{id:140406,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Repeats it back to check",desc:"Summarises what you said before responding, accurately, every time.",example:"So — Thursday, not Friday, and you'll bring the car. Yes?",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1,warm:1}},
{id:140407,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Hears names once",desc:"Retains every name on first hearing and produces it years later.",example:"Your sister's Cath, isn't it. We met at the thing in Hull.",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{warm:1,intel:1}},
{id:140408,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Tunes out anything technical",desc:"Attention visibly departs the moment a subject acquires detail.",example:"<i>(gone by the second clause)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{cur:-1,intel:-1}},
{id:140409,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Asks you to go back",desc:"Interrupts to return to something two topics earlier that hasn't been resolved.",example:"Sorry — go back. What did the letter actually say?",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{cur:1,intel:1}},
{id:140410,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Listens hardest to what isn't said",desc:"Tracks the omissions rather than the content, and usually correctly.",example:"You've not mentioned her once.",intensity:4,rarity:"signature",pol:{intel:1,emo:1}},
{id:140411,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Fully attentive for ninety seconds",desc:"Excellent, complete attention, on a short and very reliable timer.",example:"<i>(entirely present; then, precisely, not)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140412,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Hears tone before words",desc:"Responds to how something was said several beats before what was said.",example:"You're cross. — No, but you are.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:1}},
{id:140413,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Interrupts with the solution",desc:"Cuts in as soon as they have an answer, whether or not one was wanted.",example:"— just ring them. — I know, but just ring them.",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{asrt:1,emo:-1}},
{id:140414,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Attends only to the loudest person",desc:"Orients entirely to whoever has the room and misses everyone else.",example:"<i>(three people have spoken; only one was heard)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{}},
{id:140415,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Never asks a follow-up",desc:"Receives everything without ever once opening it further.",example:"Right. — <i>(and that is where it ends)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"common",pol:{cur:-1,warm:-1}},
{id:140416,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Listens over their shoulder",desc:"Tracks the conversation behind them while nominally in this one.",example:"<i>(head still, attention entirely at the next table)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{cur:1,man:-1}},
{id:140417,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Hums to show they're following",desc:"A continuous low stream of acknowledgement noises throughout.",example:"Mm. Mm-hm. Mm.",intensity:1,rarity:"common",pol:{warm:1}},
{id:140418,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Remembers the wrong detail",desc:"Retains something small and peripheral and loses the substance entirely.",example:"You were wearing the blue thing. — No, I don't remember what you said.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140419,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Refuses to be told twice",desc:"Cuts off any repetition sharply, which makes people stop explaining.",example:"You've said. — You've said that.",intensity:4,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{agr:-1,man:-1}},
{id:140420,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Goes quiet to make room",desc:"Deliberately withdraws from a conversation so a quieter person can enter it.",example:"<i>(stops mid-thought and looks at the person who hasn't spoken)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{warm:1,man:1}},
{id:140421,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Reconstructs it later, wrongly",desc:"Listens well and files it inaccurately, confidently, forever.",example:"You definitely said Tuesday. — You did. I remember it clearly.",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140422,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Attention drops at their own name",desc:"Being addressed directly is the thing that breaks their concentration.",example:"Sorry — what? No, I heard everything up to that.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{}},
{id:140423,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Cannot listen and be looked at",desc:"Takes things in far better side by side than face to face.",example:"<i>(turns to face the road; is now listening properly)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:-1}},
{id:140424,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Loudly performs listening",desc:"Enormous, unmissable signals of attention that crowd out the speaker.",example:"RIGHT. YES. GO ON. I'M LISTENING.",intensity:5,rarity:"common",pol:{vol:1,warm:1}},
{id:140425,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Hears the whole thing, answers days later",desc:"Nothing at the time and a complete, considered response much later.",example:"<i>(Thursday)</i> — about what you said on Monday.",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{pace:-1,intel:1}},
{id:140426,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Attention snapped by any screen",desc:"A television anywhere in the room takes them completely, mid-sentence.",example:"— sorry, what was — <i>(gone again)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{cur:-1,man:-1}},
{id:140427,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Listens to instructions once, exactly",desc:"Full attention for the duration, no repetition needed, ever.",example:"<i>(gets it right the first time and does not ask again)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1,disc:1}},
{id:140428,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Answers the emotion, not the content",desc:"Responds to what the speaker feels and lets the facts go past.",example:"\"...so the letter came on Friday.\" \"That must have been horrible.\"",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:1,warm:1}},
{id:140429,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Overwhelmed by two speakers",desc:"Two voices at once is not difficult but impossible, and visibly so.",example:"<i>(a hand up)</i> One. One at a time.",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{intel:-1}},
{id:140430,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Never once interrupts",desc:"Absolute, total floor-yielding, to everyone, at all times.",example:"<i>(has waited eleven minutes and will keep waiting)</i>",intensity:5,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{asrt:-1,man:1}},
{id:140431,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Watches the room, not the speaker",desc:"Attention is on everyone's reaction rather than on the person talking.",example:"<i>(scanning faces while somebody explains something)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1}},
{id:140432,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Blank, and heard every word",desc:"Gives no feedback of any kind and can reproduce the whole thing verbatim.",example:"<i>(nothing at all)</i> — you said four thirty, and then you said 'if he turns up'.",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:-1,intel:1}},
{id:140433,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Leans in for bad news only",desc:"Ordinary attention throughout and total focus the moment something goes wrong.",example:"<i>(chair forward, suddenly)</i> — say that again.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{}},
{id:140434,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Finishes listening early",desc:"Decides they have the point and audibly moves on while you are still talking.",example:"Yep, got it, so what we'll do is —",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{asrt:1,man:-1}},
{id:140435,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Hears one word and stops",desc:"A single trigger word ends their attention for the rest of the conversation.",example:"<i>(the word was 'mother'; nothing after it arrived)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:1}},
{id:140436,section:"Mannerisms",category:"Listening & Attention",trait:"Silent, and remembers it for years",desc:"Says nothing at the time and produces it, exactly, a decade later.",example:"You told me this in 2011. In the car.",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{intel:1}},

/* ================================================================
   6. THE MATCHING POSITIVE POLES
   ----------------------------------------------------------------
   The variant fill above lands entirely on three negative-pole
   categories, which pushed Confidence, Emotional Capacity and
   Intelligence past the suite's "both poles within 25%" invariant.
   That invariant is the right one — a lopsided axis means pushing a
   slider one way gives you materially more material than the other,
   which is precisely the complaint this file exists to answer — so
   the fix is to author the other side rather than relax the check.
   These also carry the positive-side depth those three axes need at
   the tails, where all three were thin.
   ================================================================ */

/* ---------- Confidence — Self-Assured ---------- */
{id:140500,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Asks the basic question",desc:"Will say they don't know something in front of people who assume they do.",example:"Sorry — what does that acronym actually stand for?",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{ego:1,cur:1}},
{id:140501,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Takes the smaller role",desc:"Steps back from the visible job without any sense of loss.",example:"You run it. I'll do the boring half.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{ego:1,man:1}},
{id:140502,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Registers disapproval and moves on",desc:"Hears that someone thinks badly of them and is genuinely unaffected.",example:"I know. He's entitled to think that.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{ego:1,emo:-1}},
{id:140503,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Doesn't explain the decision",desc:"Announces what they're doing and feels no need to justify it.",example:"I'm not coming. — No, that's just the answer.",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{ego:1,asrt:1}},
{id:140504,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Praises rivals accurately",desc:"Gives full, specific credit to people they are competing with.",example:"She's better at this than I am. That's just true.",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{ego:1,hon:1}},
{id:140505,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Repeats themselves without embarrassment",desc:"Says the thing again, plainly, when it wasn't heard.",example:"I'll say it again because it matters.",intensity:2,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{ego:1,asrt:1}},
{id:140506,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Unhurried under scrutiny",desc:"Takes as long as they need with everyone watching.",example:"<i>(reads the whole page while the room waits)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{ego:1,pace:-1}},
{id:140507,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Wears the wrong thing happily",desc:"Notices they've misjudged the dress code and does not mind at all.",example:"Bit casual, aren't I. Never mind.",intensity:2,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140508,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Says 'I don't know' first",desc:"Leads with the limit of their knowledge rather than around it.",example:"I don't know. I could find out by Thursday.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{ego:1,hon:1}},
{id:140509,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Eats alone in public",desc:"Entirely at ease being visibly unaccompanied.",example:"<i>(a book, a full meal, the window table)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140510,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Doesn't check the room after speaking",desc:"Says their piece and does not scan for how it landed.",example:"<i>(already looking at the agenda again)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140511,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Accepts a compliment plainly",desc:"Says thank you and stops, with no deflection at all.",example:"Thank you. That one took a while to get right.",intensity:2,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{ego:1,hon:1}},
{id:140512,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Asks for what they want directly",desc:"States the request without a preamble or an escape route.",example:"I'd like the Tuesday off.",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:1,asrt:1}},
{id:140513,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Steady when contradicted publicly",desc:"Absorbs a challenge in front of others without any change of temperature.",example:"Could be. Say more.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{ego:1,agr:1}},
{id:140514,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Leaves when they want to leave",desc:"Goes at the point they'd like to, without engineering a reason.",example:"Right, I'm off. Lovely to see you all.",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140515,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Never rehearses a phone call",desc:"Rings without preparing what to say, on anything.",example:"<i>(dials mid-sentence)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{ego:1}},
{id:140516,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Sits with the silence they caused",desc:"Says a hard thing and does not rush to fill the gap after it.",example:"<i>(said it; waits)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{ego:1,asrt:1}},
{id:140517,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Changes their mind out loud",desc:"Revises a stated position publicly and without any face-saving.",example:"I've thought about it and I was wrong on Tuesday.",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{ego:1,hon:1}},
{id:140518,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Unbothered by silence in company",desc:"Comfortable saying nothing for long stretches with other people present.",example:"<i>(twenty minutes, both reading, entirely fine)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:1,vol:-1}},
{id:140519,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Argues loudly and lets it go",desc:"Full-volume disagreement, over instantly, no residue at all.",example:"Right, that's rubbish and you know it. — Anyway. Pint?",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:1,vol:1}},
{id:140520,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Announces their rate without flinching",desc:"States what they cost, plainly, and does not soften it.",example:"Four hundred. — Yes.",intensity:4,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{ego:1,asrt:1}},
{id:140521,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Takes the criticism and keeps going",desc:"Absorbs a serious note, adjusts, and does not need reassurance after.",example:"That's fair. I'll redo the second half.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{ego:1,disc:1}},
{id:140522,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Entirely certain, in one narrow field",desc:"Modest about everything except a single thing they genuinely know.",example:"On most of this I'd defer. Not on the wiring.",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{ego:1,intel:1}},
{id:140523,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Introduces themselves first",desc:"Crosses the room to a stranger without any visible cost.",example:"Hello — I don't think we've met.",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{ego:1,warm:1}},
{id:140524,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Confidence — Self-Assured",trait:"Refuses without a reason",desc:"Declines cleanly and offers no justification, and it isn't rude.",example:"No, thank you. <i>(and that is the whole answer)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{ego:1,asrt:1}},

/* ---------- Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep ---------- */
{id:140530,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Names the feeling as it arrives",desc:"Reports internal weather in real time, accurately and without drama.",example:"I've gone defensive. Give me a second.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:1,hon:1}},
{id:140531,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Sits with someone else's grief",desc:"Stays in the room without fixing, advising, or leaving.",example:"<i>(pulls the chair round and says nothing for a long time)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:1,warm:1}},
{id:140532,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Admits to being frightened",desc:"Says the vulnerable thing plainly, in the moment, out loud.",example:"I'm scared about Thursday. That's all it is.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:1,hon:1}},
{id:140533,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Remembers how things felt",desc:"Recalls the emotional texture of events as precisely as the facts.",example:"It was the waiting. The room smelled of floor polish.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:1}},
{id:140534,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Says the affectionate thing",desc:"Voices fondness directly rather than implying it, to everyone.",example:"I'm very glad you're here. I mean that.",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{emo:1,warm:1}},
{id:140535,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Notices the room's mood first",desc:"Reads the emotional temperature before anyone has said anything.",example:"Something's happened. — Something has, though.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:1,intel:1}},
{id:140536,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Lets the sentence break",desc:"Keeps going through a voice that has stopped working properly.",example:"— sorry — <i>(carries on anyway)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:1}},
{id:140537,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Asks how it actually was",desc:"Presses gently past the first polite answer, every time.",example:"No — how was it really.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:1,cur:1}},
{id:140538,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Moved by strangers' good news",desc:"Genuinely, visibly affected by things that have nothing to do with them.",example:"<i>(reading a notice in a window, quite undone)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{emo:1,pos:1}},
{id:140539,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Says sorry and means the specific thing",desc:"Apologises with the exact injury named rather than in general.",example:"I'm sorry I said that about your father in front of them.",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:1,hon:1}},
{id:140540,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Holds two feelings at once",desc:"Reports contradictory emotions without needing to resolve them.",example:"I'm relieved and I'm furious. Both. All the time.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:1,intel:1}},
{id:140541,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Cries and keeps making sense",desc:"Full emotion and full articulacy running at the same time.",example:"<i>(crying)</i> — and the second thing is that I don't trust him.",intensity:4,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:1}},
{id:140542,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Physically affectionate without asking",desc:"Reaches for people naturally and reads correctly who wants it.",example:"<i>(a hand on the shoulder, exactly long enough)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{emo:1,warm:1}},
{id:140543,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Tells you what they need",desc:"States the requirement directly rather than hoping it's inferred.",example:"I need you to just agree with me for ten minutes.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:1,asrt:1}},
{id:140544,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Stays angry visibly and briefly",desc:"Fully expressed, fully finished, nothing carried forward.",example:"I'm furious with you. — <i>(twenty minutes later)</i> — right, food?",intensity:4,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{emo:1,vol:1}},
{id:140545,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Describes the feeling physically",desc:"Locates emotions in the body and reports where they are.",example:"It's behind the ribs. It's been there since Tuesday.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:1}},
{id:140546,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Doesn't flinch from the hard sentence",desc:"Says the thing that will hurt them to say, and says it whole.",example:"I think I stopped loving you in about 2019.",intensity:5,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:1,hon:1}},
{id:140547,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Laughs and cries in the same minute",desc:"Moves between registers fast and completely, without performance.",example:"<i>(both, at once, at the photograph)</i>",intensity:4,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:1}},
{id:140548,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Talks about the dead easily",desc:"Brings them up naturally, in the present, without lowering the room.",example:"Dad would have absolutely hated this carpet.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:1,warm:1}},
{id:140549,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Asks to be comforted",desc:"Requests it outright rather than waiting to be noticed.",example:"Can you just — for a minute. Yeah. That.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:1,asrt:1}},
{id:140550,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Openly delighted by small things",desc:"Full, unembarrassed pleasure at things adults are supposed to be past.",example:"<i>(genuinely thrilled about the heron)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"common",pol:{emo:1,pos:1}},
{id:140551,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Says when they've been hurt",desc:"Reports the injury at the time rather than storing it.",example:"That one landed. I want you to know it landed.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{emo:1,hon:1}},
{id:140552,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Weeps at music in company",desc:"Entirely unguarded, in public, at something everyone else is enjoying calmly.",example:"<i>(four bars in, gone, and not hiding it)</i>",intensity:5,rarity:"common",pol:{emo:1}},
{id:140553,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Emotional Capacity — Expressive & Deep",trait:"Forgives out loud and completely",desc:"Says it plainly, once, and then genuinely acts as though it's finished.",example:"That's done. I'm not carrying it.",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{emo:1,warm:1}},

/* ---------- Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical ---------- */
{id:140560,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Restates the problem better",desc:"Reformulates what's being discussed so the answer becomes obvious.",example:"So it's not a money question. It's a who-decides question.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1}},
{id:140561,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Notices what changed",desc:"Spots the one altered variable in a familiar situation immediately.",example:"You've moved the timings. That's what's different.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1,cur:1}},
{id:140562,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Asks what would change their mind",desc:"Names their own falsifier before arguing, as a matter of habit.",example:"If the March figures come back flat, I'm wrong. Let's look at March.",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{intel:1,hon:1}},
{id:140563,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Holds the whole structure in mind",desc:"Tracks a complicated thing entire, with no notes, for a long time.",example:"...which is why the third clause contradicts the appendix.",intensity:4,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1}},
{id:140564,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Separates the two questions",desc:"Splits a tangled disagreement into its actually-separate parts.",example:"Whether it's fair and whether it's legal are different arguments.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1}},
{id:140565,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Estimates well, quickly",desc:"Produces an approximation that turns out to be close, without working.",example:"Call it eleven thousand. — <i>(it was 10,800)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{intel:1}},
{id:140566,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Quietly rebuilds the argument",desc:"Reconstructs the other person's case more strongly before answering it.",example:"Your best version of that is stronger than the one you gave. Take that one.",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{intel:1,man:1}},
{id:140567,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Reads the footnote",desc:"Goes to the part nobody reads and finds the thing that matters there.",example:"It's in the schedule at the back. Page forty.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1,cur:1}},
{id:140568,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Catches the buried assumption",desc:"Names the unstated premise everyone in the room has been standing on.",example:"We've all assumed he wants the job. Has anyone asked?",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1}},
{id:140569,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Explains it once, precisely",desc:"Pitches the explanation exactly right first time and does not repeat it.",example:"<i>(three sentences; everybody has it)</i>",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{intel:1,vol:-1}},
{id:140570,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Tracks the inconsistency across weeks",desc:"Remembers a claim from a month ago and notices it has quietly changed.",example:"In March you said the opposite of that.",intensity:4,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1,hon:1}},
{id:140571,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Builds the small model first",desc:"Tries the simplest version of anything before committing to the real one.",example:"Let's do it with three and see what breaks.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1,disc:1}},
{id:140572,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Distrusts their own first answer",desc:"Reflexively checks the thing that came to them immediately.",example:"That was too quick. Let me look again.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1,disc:1}},
{id:140573,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Reads the room analytically",desc:"Works out the social situation as a structure rather than feeling it.",example:"She's the one who decides. He's the one who'll object.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1,emo:-1}},
{id:140574,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Finds the cheapest test",desc:"Identifies the smallest experiment that would settle the disagreement.",example:"Ring them. That's a two-minute answer to an hour of this.",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{intel:1,disc:1}},
{id:140575,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Sharp about their own bias",desc:"Names the reason they might be wrong about this one specifically.",example:"I want it to be true, which is exactly why I don't trust me on it.",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{intel:1,hon:1}},
{id:140576,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Sees the pattern in three examples",desc:"Generalises fast and correctly from very little.",example:"That's happened three times. It's the Friday handover.",intensity:3,rarity:"uncommon",pol:{intel:1}},
{id:140577,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Refuses the false choice",desc:"Rejects the two options offered and produces a third.",example:"It's not either. There's a version where we do neither.",intensity:4,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1,agr:-1}},
{id:140578,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Precise about what they don't know",desc:"Maps the edge of their own knowledge exactly rather than vaguely.",example:"I know the mechanism. I don't know the dosing. Ask someone else about dosing.",intensity:2,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1,hon:1}},
{id:140579,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Analyses aloud at length",desc:"Full, unmissable, sustained reasoning delivered to whoever is present.",example:"Right, so there are four ways this goes, and the first one is —",intensity:4,rarity:"common",pol:{intel:1,vol:1}},
{id:140580,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Quietly right, weeks early",desc:"Reached the conclusion long before and mentioned it to nobody.",example:"Mm. — <i>(had written it down in January)</i>",intensity:2,rarity:"signature",pol:{intel:1,vol:-1}},
{id:140581,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Cross-examines relentlessly",desc:"Large, sustained, unmistakable interrogation of a weak claim.",example:"How do you know that? — And how do THEY know that?",intensity:5,rarity:"common",pol:{intel:1,agr:-1}},
{id:140582,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Corrects themselves mid-argument",desc:"Notices their own error while making the case and says so at once.",example:"— no, that's wrong, I've got the years the wrong way round.",intensity:3,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1,hon:1}},
{id:140583,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Learns a whole field in a fortnight",desc:"Goes from nothing to genuinely competent, fast, and repeatedly.",example:"Two weeks ago I'd never heard of it. Ask me anything.",intensity:4,rarity:"distinctive",pol:{intel:1,cur:1}},
{id:140584,section:"Personality Traits",category:"Intelligence — Sharp & Analytical",trait:"Notices the missing number",desc:"Spots what has been left out of a set of figures rather than what's in it.",example:"There's no line for the deposits. Where are the deposits?",intensity:3,rarity:"signature",pol:{intel:1}},
];

TRAITS.push(...TRAITS_BALANCE);
